// GENERATED by tools/build-content.mjs. Do not edit; change content/content.mjs and run `npm run content`.
export const LINES = [{"id":"L1","zh":"破冰","en":"Breaking the ice"},{"id":"L2","zh":"校园","en":"Student life"},{"id":"L3","zh":"求职","en":"The job hunt"},{"id":"L4","zh":"面试","en":"Interviews & offers"},{"id":"L5","zh":"分析","en":"Talking analytics"}];
export const SCENES = [{"id":"s1","line":"L1","zh":"最近怎么样","en":"First hello","who":"小雨","setup":"Xiaoyu, a first-year who arrived two months ago, turns up early for her first appointment.","culture":"Students call staff 老师 whether or not you teach. It is plain respect, and you can simply accept it. 还行吧 is rarely \"fine\": listen for the 就是… that follows.","lines":[{"s":"S","zh":"老师好！我是不是来早了？","en":"Hello! Am I early?"},{"s":"T","zh":"没事没事，快请进，随便坐。","en":"Not at all. Come on in, sit anywhere."},{"s":"S","zh":"谢谢老师。","en":"Thank you."},{"s":"T","zh":"来这边两个月了吧？还适应吗？","en":"It's been about two months, right? Settling in OK?"},{"s":"S","zh":"还行吧，就是时差倒了好久，课也挺紧的。","en":"It's OK, I guess. The jet lag took forever, and classes are pretty intense."},{"s":"T","zh":"刚开始都这样，慢慢来。这边的饭吃得惯吗？","en":"It's always like that at first. Take your time. Are you used to the food here?"},{"s":"S","zh":"说实话，不太习惯，天天想我妈做的菜。","en":"Honestly, not really. I miss my mom's cooking every day."},{"s":"T","zh":"哈哈，那肯定的。想家的时候，就多跟家里视频视频。","en":"Ha, of course. When you get homesick, video-call home more often."},{"s":"S","zh":"嗯，几乎每个周末都视频。老师，您的中文怎么这么好？","en":"Yeah, almost every weekend. How is your Chinese so good?"},{"s":"T","zh":"哪里哪里，好久没说，都生疏了。今天正好跟你练练。","en":"Oh, hardly. I haven't spoken it in ages and it's gone rusty. Today's a good chance to practice with you."}],"qs":[{"q":"小雨说“还行吧”，她的意思最可能是什么？","opts":["过得去，但其实有点儿辛苦","一切都非常顺利","她很不喜欢这里"],"why":"还行吧 + 就是… is classic understatement: fine on the surface, with a \"but\" on its way."},{"q":"小雨最想念什么？","opts":["妈妈做的菜","国内的朋友","上海的天气"],"why":"天天想我妈做的菜. Food is usually the first thing students miss."}],"chunks":[{"zh":"随便坐。","en":"Sit anywhere, make yourself comfortable.","note":"Warm and casual. Pairs naturally with 快请进.","ex":["你先","随便","坐一下，","我","马上就来。"],"exEn":"Have a seat for a moment, I'll be right there.","id":"随便坐。","scene":"s1"},{"zh":"还适应吗？","en":"Settling in OK?","note":"适应 = to adjust. Lighter than 习惯了吗, and the standard thing to ask a newcomer.","ex":["来这边","都","两个月了，","生活上","还适应吗？"],"exEn":"You've been here two months now. Adjusting OK to life here?","id":"还适应吗？","scene":"s1"},{"zh":"时差倒了好久。","en":"It took me ages to get over the jet lag.","note":"倒时差 dǎo shíchā is verb + object, so the two can split: 时差还没倒过来.","ex":["我的时差到现在","还没","倒过来。"],"exEn":"I still haven't got over my jet lag.","id":"时差倒了好久。","scene":"s1"},{"zh":"刚开始都这样，慢慢来。","en":"It's always like this at first. Take it slowly.","note":"慢慢来 is the all-purpose reassurance: no rush, it will come.","ex":["别着急，","刚开始","都这样，","过一阵子","就好了。"],"exEn":"Don't worry, it's always like this at first. It'll be fine after a while.","id":"刚开始都这样，慢慢来。","scene":"s1"},{"zh":"吃得惯吗？","en":"Are you used to the food?","note":"Verb + 得惯 / 不惯: 住得惯, 看不惯, 听不惯.","ex":["学校食堂的饭，","你现在","吃得惯","了吗？"],"exEn":"Are you used to the cafeteria food by now?","id":"吃得惯吗？","scene":"s1"},{"zh":"那肯定的。","en":"Well, of course.","note":"Warm agreement with something obvious.","ex":["第一次","离开家","这么远，","想家","是肯定的。"],"exEn":"First time this far from home. Of course you get homesick.","id":"那肯定的。","scene":"s1"},{"zh":"哪里哪里，都生疏了。","en":"Oh, hardly. It's gone rusty.","note":"Deflect a compliment before anything else. 生疏 shēngshū = rusty from disuse.","ex":["我的中文","十几年","没用，","早就","生疏了。"],"exEn":"I haven't used my Chinese in over ten years. It went rusty long ago.","id":"哪里哪里，都生疏了。","scene":"s1"}]},{"id":"s2","line":"L1","zh":"老家哪里的","en":"Where's home?","who":"浩然","setup":"Haoran notices the photo of Shanghai on your desk.","culture":"你老家是哪儿的 is the single best icebreaker. Hometown identity runs deep, and every city has a dish it is proud of. Praise the food.","lines":[{"s":"S","zh":"老师，这张照片是在外滩拍的吧？","en":"Was this photo taken on the Bund?"},{"s":"T","zh":"对，眼睛真尖！我在上海待过两年。","en":"Yes, sharp eyes! I lived in Shanghai for two years."},{"s":"S","zh":"真的假的？怪不得您中文说得这么地道。","en":"Seriously? No wonder your Chinese sounds so natural."},{"s":"T","zh":"过奖了，学的那点儿东西早就还给老师了。你老家是哪儿的？","en":"You flatter me. What little I learned I've long since forgotten. Where's your hometown?"},{"s":"S","zh":"我是苏州人，离上海特别近，高铁半个小时就到了。","en":"I'm from Suzhou, really close to Shanghai. Half an hour by high-speed rail."},{"s":"T","zh":"苏州好地方啊！我去过一次，园林特别漂亮。","en":"Suzhou, lovely place! I've been once. The gardens are beautiful."},{"s":"S","zh":"那您肯定吃过生煎吧？","en":"Then you must have had shengjian buns?"},{"s":"T","zh":"当然，一说起来我就馋了。这边有没有正宗一点儿的中餐馆？","en":"Of course. Just talking about them makes me hungry. Is there a reasonably authentic Chinese restaurant around here?"},{"s":"S","zh":"有一家还不错，下次我带您去。","en":"There's one that's pretty good. I'll take you next time."},{"s":"T","zh":"那就这么说定了！","en":"Then it's a deal!"}],"qs":[{"q":"浩然为什么说“怪不得”？","opts":["他明白了老师中文好的原因","他觉得老师很奇怪","他不相信老师去过上海"],"why":"怪不得 = \"no wonder\". Something has just made sense."},{"q":"“还给老师了”是什么意思？","opts":["学过的东西都忘了","把书还给了老师","回去看老师了"],"why":"A stock joke: what you learned went straight back to the teacher."},{"q":"从苏州坐高铁到上海要多久？","opts":["半个小时","两个小时","一个半小时"],"why":"高铁半个小时就到了."}],"chunks":[{"zh":"我在上海待过两年。","en":"I lived in Shanghai for two years.","note":"待 dāi + 过 for a past stint somewhere. More colloquial than 住过.","ex":["我年轻的时候","在上海","待过","两年。"],"exEn":"I spent two years in Shanghai when I was young.","id":"我在上海待过两年。","scene":"s2"},{"zh":"怪不得！","en":"No wonder!","note":"For the moment something suddenly makes sense. Often followed by 原来….","ex":["怪不得","你","对上海","这么熟，","原来","在那儿住过。"],"exEn":"No wonder you know Shanghai so well. So you lived there.","id":"怪不得！","scene":"s2"},{"zh":"过奖了。","en":"You flatter me.","note":"The modest reply to praise. A notch more formal than 哪里哪里.","ex":["您","过奖了，","我","还差得远呢。"],"exEn":"You flatter me. I've still got a long way to go.","id":"过奖了。","scene":"s2"},{"zh":"早就还给老师了。","en":"I've long since forgotten it all.","note":"Literally \"gave it back to the teacher\". Reliable for a laugh.","ex":["大学学的","那点儿统计，","我","早就","还给老师了。"],"exEn":"The bit of statistics I learned in college, I've long since forgotten.","id":"早就还给老师了。","scene":"s2"},{"zh":"你老家是哪儿的？","en":"Where's your hometown?","note":"老家 = where your family is from. Warmer than 你是哪里人.","ex":["听口音，","你老家","是","南方的","吧？"],"exEn":"From your accent, you're from the south, right?","id":"你老家是哪儿的？","scene":"s2"},{"zh":"一说起来我就馋了。","en":"Just talking about it makes me hungry.","note":"一…就… = as soon as. 馋 chán = craving food.","ex":["一","说起","小笼包，","我","就","馋了。"],"exEn":"The moment anyone mentions soup dumplings, I get a craving.","id":"一说起来我就馋了。","scene":"s2"},{"zh":"那就这么说定了！","en":"Then it's a deal!","note":"Seals a casual plan.","ex":["下次","你带我去，","咱们","就这么","说定了。"],"exEn":"Next time you take me there. That's settled.","id":"那就这么说定了！","scene":"s2"}]},{"id":"s13","line":"L1","zh":"回家过年吗","en":"Home for New Year?","who":"思琪","setup":"Late January. You run into Siqi in the hallway just before the Lunar New Year.","culture":"春晚, the Spring Festival Gala, is watched and roasted online by hundreds of millions. Homophone luck is everywhere: 鱼 sounds like 余 (surplus). A New Year greeting from you will be remembered.","lines":[{"s":"T","zh":"思琪，快过年了，今年回国吗？","en":"Siqi, New Year's nearly here. Going back to China this year?"},{"s":"S","zh":"回不去，机票太贵了，而且刚开学，请不了假。","en":"Can't. Flights are too expensive, and term has just started, so I can't take time off."},{"s":"T","zh":"那年夜饭怎么办？总不能一个人吃泡面吧？","en":"Then what about New Year's Eve dinner? You can't just eat instant noodles on your own, surely?"},{"s":"S","zh":"不会啦，我们几个同学约好了一起包饺子、看春晚。","en":"No, no. A few of us have arranged to make dumplings and watch the Gala together."},{"s":"T","zh":"那挺热闹的。你家里过年有什么讲究吗？","en":"That'll be lively. Does your family have any New Year customs?"},{"s":"S","zh":"我们家年三十一定要吃鱼，年年有余嘛。还有，长辈会给小孩儿发红包。","en":"In our family we have to eat fish on New Year's Eve. Surplus every year, you know. And the elders give the kids red envelopes."},{"s":"T","zh":"你现在还收得到红包吗？","en":"Do you still get red envelopes?"},{"s":"S","zh":"哈哈，工作以前都能收。等我上班了，就该我给别人发了。","en":"Ha, you get them until you start working. Once I have a job, it'll be my turn to give them."},{"s":"T","zh":"原来是这样。那我提前给你拜个早年，祝你新的一年万事如意！","en":"So that's how it works. Then let me wish you an early Happy New Year. May everything go your way!"},{"s":"S","zh":"谢谢老师！也祝您新年快乐，身体健康！","en":"Thank you! Happy New Year to you too, and good health!"}],"qs":[{"q":"思琪今年为什么不回国过年？","opts":["机票太贵，而且请不了假","她不想家","她要去旅行"],"why":"机票太贵了，而且刚开学，请不了假."},{"q":"过年为什么要吃鱼？","opts":["“鱼”和“余”同音，表示年年有余","鱼很便宜","思琪最爱吃鱼"],"why":"年年有余: 鱼 yú sounds like 余 yú, surplus."}],"chunks":[{"zh":"快过年了，今年回国吗？","en":"New Year's nearly here. Going home this year?","note":"快…了 = about to. 过年 means the Lunar New Year specifically.","ex":["快","过年了，","你今年","回不回国？"],"exEn":"New Year's almost here. Are you going back this year?","id":"快过年了，今年回国吗？","scene":"s13"},{"zh":"总不能一个人吃泡面吧？","en":"You can't just eat instant noodles on your own, surely?","note":"总不能…吧 = \"surely you can't…\". Caring and a little teasing.","ex":["大过年的，","你","总不能","一个人","吃泡面吧？"],"exEn":"It's New Year! You can't eat instant noodles alone, surely?","id":"总不能一个人吃泡面吧？","scene":"s13"},{"zh":"那挺热闹的。","en":"That'll be lively.","note":"热闹 rènao is a real positive. Its opposite, 冷清, is sad.","ex":["十几个人","一起","包饺子，","肯定","挺热闹的。"],"exEn":"A dozen people making dumplings together. That's bound to be lively.","id":"那挺热闹的。","scene":"s13"},{"zh":"有什么讲究吗？","en":"Are there any particular customs?","note":"讲究 jiǎngjiu = the things one is careful to do right.","ex":["你们家过年","有","什么讲究","吗？"],"exEn":"Does your family have any New Year customs?","id":"有什么讲究吗？","scene":"s13"},{"zh":"原来是这样。","en":"Oh, so that's how it is.","note":"原来 marks a discovery: now I see.","ex":["原来","是这样，","怪不得","大家","都","爱吃鱼。"],"exEn":"So that's why. No wonder everyone eats fish.","id":"原来是这样。","scene":"s13"},{"zh":"给你拜个早年。","en":"Wishing you an early Happy New Year.","note":"拜年 = pay a New Year call. 拜个早年 is for when you will not see them on the day.","ex":["过年","见不着，","我","提前","给你","拜个早年。"],"exEn":"I won't see you at New Year, so here's an early greeting.","id":"给你拜个早年。","scene":"s13"},{"zh":"祝你万事如意！","en":"May everything go the way you wish!","note":"Blessings come in fours: 万事如意, 身体健康, 心想事成, 恭喜发财.","ex":["祝你","新的一年","工作顺利，","万事如意！"],"exEn":"Wishing you smooth work and every success in the new year!","id":"祝你万事如意！","scene":"s13"}]},{"id":"s3","line":"L2","zh":"卷不动了","en":"Burned out","who":"思琪","setup":"Midterm season. Siqi looks exhausted.","culture":"内卷 nèijuǎn, \"involution\", went mainstream around 2020 and was soon clipped to 卷. 躺平 (\"lying flat\") is the counter-move, 摆烂 (\"letting it rot\") its bleaker cousin. Students say all three half-joking. Match the humour before you advise.","lines":[{"s":"T","zh":"思琪，你看起来有点儿累，最近是不是没休息好？","en":"Siqi, you look a bit tired. Not getting enough rest lately?"},{"s":"S","zh":"唉，别提了，这学期太卷了。","en":"Ugh, don't ask. This semester is so cutthroat."},{"s":"T","zh":"怎么个卷法？说来听听。","en":"Cutthroat how? Tell me about it."},{"s":"S","zh":"我们班同学一个比一个拼，有人已经刷了三百道题了，我才刚开始。","en":"Everyone in my class pushes harder than the next. Someone has already ground through three hundred practice problems, and I've barely started."},{"s":"T","zh":"听起来压力挺大的。你自己呢，是怎么打算的？","en":"That sounds like a lot of pressure. And you, what's your plan?"},{"s":"S","zh":"我也不知道，有时候真想躺平算了。","en":"I don't know. Sometimes I just want to give up and lie flat."},{"s":"T","zh":"偶尔想躺平很正常，别跟别人比，按自己的节奏来。","en":"Wanting to lie flat now and then is normal. Don't compare yourself with others. Go at your own pace."},{"s":"S","zh":"道理我都懂，可是一刷朋友圈就焦虑。","en":"I know all that. But the moment I scroll through Moments, I get anxious."},{"s":"T","zh":"那就少刷一点儿。这个周末给自己放个假，好好睡一觉。","en":"Then scroll a little less. Give yourself this weekend off and get a proper sleep."},{"s":"S","zh":"好，听您的。跟您聊完，心里舒服多了。","en":"OK, I'll do that. I feel a lot better after talking with you."}],"qs":[{"q":"思琪说的“卷”是什么意思？","opts":["同学之间竞争太激烈","作业太简单","她想换专业"],"why":"卷 = everyone competing harder and harder for the same prize."},{"q":"什么事会让思琪更焦虑？","opts":["刷朋友圈","跟老师聊天儿","周末睡觉"],"why":"一刷朋友圈就焦虑: other people's highlight reels."}],"chunks":[{"zh":"别提了。","en":"Ugh, don't ask.","note":"Signals that it has been rough, and invites you to ask anyway.","ex":["别提了，","我昨天","熬夜","熬到","三点。"],"exEn":"Don't ask. I was up until three last night.","id":"别提了。","scene":"s3"},{"zh":"太卷了。","en":"It's so cutthroat.","note":"From 内卷 nèijuǎn. Also a verb: 卷不动了 = I can't keep up the grind.","ex":["现在","找实习","也","越来越","卷了。"],"exEn":"Even finding an internship is getting more and more cutthroat.","id":"太卷了。","scene":"s3"},{"zh":"说来听听。","en":"Tell me about it, let's hear it.","note":"An easy, low-pressure way to get someone talking.","ex":["你","有什么想法，","说来","听听。"],"exEn":"Whatever you're thinking, let's hear it.","id":"说来听听。","scene":"s3"},{"zh":"你是怎么打算的？","en":"What's your plan?","note":"Asks for their thinking without pushing yours. 是…的 softens it.","ex":["毕业以后，","你","是","怎么","打算的？"],"exEn":"What are you planning to do after graduation?","id":"你是怎么打算的？","scene":"s3"},{"zh":"真想躺平算了。","en":"I just want to give up and coast.","note":"躺平 = opt out of the rat race. …算了 = might as well just.","ex":["太累了，","有时候","真想","躺平","算了。"],"exEn":"I'm so tired. Sometimes I just want to lie flat and be done with it.","id":"真想躺平算了。","scene":"s3"},{"zh":"按自己的节奏来。","en":"Go at your own pace.","note":"按…来 = do it according to…","ex":["别","跟别人比，","按","自己的节奏","来。"],"exEn":"Don't compare yourself with others. Go at your own pace.","id":"按自己的节奏来。","scene":"s3"},{"zh":"道理我都懂，可是……","en":"I know all that in theory, but…","note":"The object comes first. The standard way to say: advice heard, feelings unchanged.","ex":["道理","我都懂，","可是","就是","做不到。"],"exEn":"I get the logic. I just can't do it.","id":"道理我都懂，可是……","scene":"s3"}]},{"id":"s4","line":"L2","zh":"搭子和社恐","en":"Finding your people","who":"子轩","setup":"Zixuan mentions that he mostly spends time with other Chinese students.","culture":"MBTI is everyday small talk among Chinese students: i人 (introvert) and e人 (extrovert) are as common as star signs. 你是i人还是e人？ is an easy opener.","lines":[{"s":"T","zh":"子轩，平时下了课都跟谁一起玩儿？","en":"Zixuan, who do you usually hang out with after class?"},{"s":"S","zh":"基本上就是我们几个中国同学，一起吃饭、打球什么的。","en":"Basically just a few of us Chinese students. We eat together, play ball, that kind of thing."},{"s":"T","zh":"有饭搭子挺好的。跟美国同学来往多吗？","en":"It's good to have meal buddies. Do you mix much with the American students?"},{"s":"S","zh":"不多。我有点儿社恐，不知道跟他们聊什么。","en":"Not much. I'm a bit socially anxious. I don't know what to talk to them about."},{"s":"T","zh":"我懂，用外语闲聊最难了，我说中文的时候也这样。","en":"I get it. Small talk in a foreign language is the hardest thing. I'm the same when I speak Chinese."},{"s":"S","zh":"真的吗？可是您看起来一点儿也不紧张。","en":"Really? But you don't look nervous at all."},{"s":"T","zh":"那是装出来的！其实不用聊什么大话题，从小组作业聊起就行。","en":"That's an act! You don't need big topics. Just start with the group project."},{"s":"S","zh":"说到小组作业，我们组有个人老是划水，我都不好意思说他。","en":"Speaking of group projects, one guy in our group is always slacking, and I feel too awkward to say anything."},{"s":"T","zh":"这种事得早点儿说开，憋在心里更难受。要不要我教你怎么开口？","en":"This kind of thing needs talking out early. Bottling it up feels worse. Want me to show you how to bring it up?"},{"s":"S","zh":"太好了，那就麻烦老师了！","en":"That would be great. Sorry to trouble you!"}],"qs":[{"q":"子轩为什么很少跟美国同学来往？","opts":["他有点儿社恐，不知道聊什么","他没有时间","美国同学不友好"],"why":"我有点儿社恐，不知道跟他们聊什么."},{"q":"“划水”的同学是什么样的人？","opts":["在小组里不怎么干活儿的人","喜欢游泳的人","做事特别快的人"],"why":"划水: paddling along while others row. A freeloader."}],"chunks":[{"zh":"平时都跟谁一起玩儿？","en":"Who do you usually hang out with?","note":"玩儿 = hang out. Adults use it too.","ex":["你周末一般","都","跟谁","一起玩儿？"],"exEn":"Who do you usually hang out with at weekends?","id":"平时都跟谁一起玩儿？","scene":"s4"},{"zh":"我想找个饭搭子。","en":"I'm looking for a meal buddy.","note":"X搭子 = a buddy for one activity: 饭搭子, 学习搭子, 健身搭子.","ex":["我刚来的时候，","连","一个饭搭子","都没有。"],"exEn":"When I first got here, I didn't have even one meal buddy.","id":"我想找个饭搭子。","scene":"s4"},{"zh":"我有点儿社恐。","en":"I'm a bit socially anxious.","note":"社恐 = 社交恐惧. The opposite is 社牛, a social powerhouse.","ex":["他","看起来","很社牛，","其实","有点儿","社恐。"],"exEn":"He looks like a social butterfly, but he's actually a bit anxious.","id":"我有点儿社恐。","scene":"s4"},{"zh":"用外语闲聊最难了。","en":"Small talk in a foreign language is the hardest.","note":"闲聊 = idle chat. Naming your own struggle puts you on their side.","ex":["对我来说，","用中文","闲聊","比","开会","还难。"],"exEn":"For me, small talk in Chinese is even harder than a meeting.","id":"用外语闲聊最难了。","scene":"s4"},{"zh":"那是装出来的。","en":"That's just an act.","note":"装 = to fake. 出来 marks the result: put on for show.","ex":["我的自信","都是","装出来的，","其实心里","很慌。"],"exEn":"My confidence is all an act. Inside I'm panicking.","id":"那是装出来的。","scene":"s4"},{"zh":"他老是划水。","en":"He's always slacking off.","note":"划水 huáshuǐ and 摸鱼 mōyú both mean coasting while others work. 老是 = always, as a complaint.","ex":["小组作业","总有人","划水，","真","让人头疼。"],"exEn":"There's always someone slacking in group projects. Such a headache.","id":"他老是划水。","scene":"s4"},{"zh":"这种事得早点儿说开。","en":"This kind of thing needs to be talked out early.","note":"得 děi = must. 说开 = get it into the open.","ex":["有矛盾","就","早点儿","说开，","别","憋在心里。"],"exEn":"If there's friction, talk it out early. Don't bottle it up.","id":"这种事得早点儿说开。","scene":"s4"}]},{"id":"s14","line":"L2","zh":"考公还是大厂","en":"Iron rice bowl or big tech","who":"浩然","setup":"Haoran says his parents are pressing him to come home and sit the civil-service exam.","culture":"体制内 (\"inside the system\": civil service and state firms) promises stability. 大厂 (big tech) pays more but brings 996 hours and the \"35-year-old crisis\". Parents who lived through instability prize the 铁饭碗. Passing the exam is 上岸, reaching shore.","lines":[{"s":"S","zh":"老师，我妈昨天又打电话催我回国考公。","en":"My mom called again yesterday, pressing me to come home and take the civil-service exam."},{"s":"T","zh":"考公？就是考公务员吧？为什么非考不可呢？","en":"考公? That's the civil-service exam, right? Why is it such a must?"},{"s":"S","zh":"在他们眼里，公务员是铁饭碗，稳定，说出去也有面子。","en":"In their eyes a civil-service job is an iron rice bowl. It's stable, and it sounds good when you tell people."},{"s":"T","zh":"那你自己想去吗？","en":"And do you want to do it?"},{"s":"S","zh":"说不好。我更想去大厂，可是听说大厂加班特别狠，三十五岁以后还可能被裁。","en":"Hard to say. I'd rather go to a big tech company, but I hear the overtime is brutal, and after thirty-five you might get laid off."},{"s":"T","zh":"所以各有各的难处。你父母是怕你太辛苦，不是不相信你。","en":"So each has its own difficulties. Your parents are afraid you'll have it too hard. It's not that they don't believe in you."},{"s":"S","zh":"这个我知道。可是每次一聊这个就吵起来。","en":"I know that. But every time we talk about it, it turns into a fight."},{"s":"T","zh":"下次别急着反驳，先听他们把话说完，再讲讲你的计划。","en":"Next time, don't rush to argue back. Hear them out first, then walk them through your plan."},{"s":"S","zh":"他们会听吗？","en":"Will they listen?"},{"s":"T","zh":"你把计划讲得越具体，他们就越放心。父母嘛，图的就是一个安心。","en":"The more concrete you make the plan, the more reassured they'll be. Parents, you know. All they want is peace of mind."},{"s":"S","zh":"有道理。等我想清楚了，再好好跟他们谈一次。","en":"That makes sense. Once I've thought it through, I'll have a proper talk with them."},{"s":"T","zh":"嗯，想清楚了随时来找我。","en":"Good. Once you've thought it through, come and find me anytime."}],"qs":[{"q":"浩然的父母为什么希望他考公？","opts":["觉得公务员稳定，也有面子","公务员工资最高","他们不喜欢美国"],"why":"公务员是铁饭碗，稳定，说出去也有面子."},{"q":"老师建议浩然下次怎么跟父母聊？","opts":["先听父母说完，再讲自己的具体计划","不接电话","马上答应考公"],"why":"别急着反驳，先听他们把话说完."}],"chunks":[{"zh":"我妈又催我回国考公。","en":"My mom's pressing me again to go home and take the civil-service exam.","note":"催 = to press or nag. 考公 = 考公务员.","ex":["一到","过年，","亲戚","就","催我","找对象。"],"exEn":"As soon as New Year comes round, the relatives press me to find a partner.","id":"我妈又催我回国考公。","scene":"s14"},{"zh":"为什么非考不可呢？","en":"Why is taking it such a must?","note":"非…不可 = absolutely must.","ex":["这场面试","很重要，","我","非去","不可。"],"exEn":"This interview matters. I absolutely have to go.","id":"为什么非考不可呢？","scene":"s14"},{"zh":"公务员是铁饭碗。","en":"A civil-service job is an iron rice bowl.","note":"铁饭碗 = a job that cannot break. 体制内 = inside the state system.","ex":["在父母眼里，","公务员","就是","铁饭碗。"],"exEn":"In parents' eyes, a civil-service job is the iron rice bowl.","id":"公务员是铁饭碗。","scene":"s14"},{"zh":"说出去也有面子。","en":"It sounds impressive when you tell people.","note":"面子 = face, standing in the eyes of others. 说出去 = when word gets out.","ex":["孩子","在大公司上班，","父母","说出去","也有面子。"],"exEn":"When their child works at a big company, parents gain face telling people.","id":"说出去也有面子。","scene":"s14"},{"zh":"说不好。","en":"Hard to say.","note":"Honest uncertainty. Softer than 不知道.","ex":["以后","留不留在美国，","现在","还","说不好。"],"exEn":"Whether I'll stay in the US, it's still hard to say.","id":"说不好。","scene":"s14"},{"zh":"各有各的难处。","en":"Each has its own difficulties.","note":"各有各的 + noun: 各有各的好处, 各有各的想法.","ex":["大厂","和","体制内，","各有","各的难处。"],"exEn":"Big tech and the state system each have their own difficulties.","id":"各有各的难处。","scene":"s14"},{"zh":"别急着反驳，先听他们把话说完。","en":"Don't rush to argue back. Hear them out first.","note":"急着 + verb = in a hurry to. 把话说完 = let them finish.","ex":["别","急着反驳，","先听","他们","把话说完。"],"exEn":"Don't rush to rebut. Let them finish first.","id":"别急着反驳，先听他们把话说完。","scene":"s14"},{"zh":"图的就是一个安心。","en":"All they want is peace of mind.","note":"图 = to be after something. 父母嘛 = parents, you know how it is.","ex":["父母","催你","回国，","图的","就是","一个安心。"],"exEn":"Parents press you to come home because all they want is peace of mind.","id":"图的就是一个安心。","scene":"s14"},{"zh":"你讲得越具体，他们就越放心。","en":"The more concrete you are, the more reassured they'll be.","note":"越…越… with two different subjects.","ex":["计划","讲得","越具体，","父母","就","越放心。"],"exEn":"The more concrete the plan, the more at ease your parents will be.","id":"你讲得越具体，他们就越放心。","scene":"s14"},{"zh":"想清楚了随时来找我。","en":"Once you've thought it through, come and find me anytime.","note":"随时 = anytime. The open door.","ex":["不着急，","你","想清楚了","随时","来找我。"],"exEn":"No rush. Come and find me whenever you've thought it through.","id":"想清楚了随时来找我。","scene":"s14"}]},{"id":"s18","line":"L2","zh":"你还好吗","en":"Are you OK?","who":"小雨","setup":"Xiaoyu has stopped coming to events and looks worn out. You check in.","culture":"Counselling still carries stigma for many students, and not letting the family worry (报喜不报忧: report the good news, hide the bad) is close to a rule. Comparing mind and body, and offering a Mandarin-speaking counsellor, lowers the barrier.","lines":[{"s":"T","zh":"小雨，最近好像不太见你来活动，一切都还好吗？","en":"Xiaoyu, I haven't seen you at events lately. Is everything all right?"},{"s":"S","zh":"还好……就是最近状态不太好，晚上老失眠。","en":"I'm OK… I just haven't been in a good place lately. I keep lying awake at night."},{"s":"T","zh":"失眠多久了？","en":"How long have you not been sleeping?"},{"s":"S","zh":"差不多两个星期了。白天没精神，上课也听不进去。","en":"About two weeks. I have no energy in the day and can't take anything in during class."},{"s":"T","zh":"听起来挺辛苦的。是不是有什么事压在心里？","en":"That sounds hard. Is something weighing on you?"},{"s":"S","zh":"找工作不顺利，又不想让家里人担心，只能一个人扛着。","en":"The job hunt isn't going well, and I don't want my family to worry, so I just carry it by myself."},{"s":"T","zh":"一个人扛着太累了。你愿意说出来，我觉得已经很不容易了。","en":"Carrying it alone is exhausting. Being willing to say it out loud is already no small thing."},{"s":"S","zh":"谢谢老师。其实说出来以后，好像轻松了一点儿。","en":"Thank you. Actually, having said it, I feel a little lighter."},{"s":"T","zh":"那就好。学校有心理咨询中心，是免费的，也有会说中文的老师。要不要我帮你约一下？","en":"I'm glad. The university has a counselling centre. It's free, and there are counsellors who speak Chinese. Shall I help you book a time?"},{"s":"S","zh":"去看心理咨询……会不会显得我很脆弱？","en":"Going to counselling… won't that make me look weak?"},{"s":"T","zh":"一点儿也不会。身体不舒服要看医生，心里不舒服找人聊聊，是一样的道理。","en":"Not in the least. When your body is unwell you see a doctor. When your mind is unwell you talk to someone. It's the same principle."},{"s":"S","zh":"那……我考虑一下。","en":"Then… I'll think about it."},{"s":"T","zh":"不着急，你什么时候想好了都可以来找我。这段时间记得按时吃饭，别硬撑。","en":"No rush. Come and find me whenever you've decided. Meanwhile, remember to eat regularly, and don't force yourself to tough it out."}],"qs":[{"q":"小雨最近怎么了？","opts":["晚上失眠，状态不好","生病住院了","找到工作了"],"why":"最近状态不太好，晚上老失眠."},{"q":"小雨为什么犹豫要不要去心理咨询？","opts":["怕显得自己很脆弱","觉得太贵","没有时间"],"why":"会不会显得我很脆弱？"}],"chunks":[{"zh":"一切都还好吗？","en":"Is everything all right?","note":"An open door, not a diagnosis. Softer than 你怎么了.","ex":["好久","没见你了，","一切","都","还好吗？"],"exEn":"I haven't seen you in ages. Is everything all right?","id":"一切都还好吗？","scene":"s18"},{"zh":"最近状态不太好。","en":"I haven't been in a good place lately.","note":"状态 = one's state or form. The usual understated way to say you are struggling.","ex":["他","最近","状态","不太好，","你","多关心一下。"],"exEn":"He hasn't been in a good place lately. Keep an eye on him.","id":"最近状态不太好。","scene":"s18"},{"zh":"晚上老失眠。","en":"I keep lying awake at night.","note":"失眠 shīmián = insomnia. 老 = keep doing, as a complaint.","ex":["压力","一大，","我","晚上","就","失眠。"],"exEn":"As soon as the pressure builds, I can't sleep at night.","id":"晚上老失眠。","scene":"s18"},{"zh":"是不是有什么事压在心里？","en":"Is something weighing on you?","note":"压在心里 = pressing on the heart.","ex":["你","是不是","有什么事","压在心里？"],"exEn":"Is something weighing on you?","id":"是不是有什么事压在心里？","scene":"s18"},{"zh":"只能一个人扛着。","en":"I just have to carry it alone.","note":"扛 káng = to shoulder a load.","ex":["有困难","别","一个人","扛着，","说出来","大家","一起想办法。"],"exEn":"Don't shoulder a problem alone. Say it, and we'll work it out together.","id":"只能一个人扛着。","scene":"s18"},{"zh":"你愿意说出来，已经很不容易了。","en":"Being willing to say it is already no small thing.","note":"不容易 as praise: that took something.","ex":["你","能","坚持到现在，","已经","很不容易了。"],"exEn":"You've kept going this long. That is no small thing.","id":"你愿意说出来，已经很不容易了。","scene":"s18"},{"zh":"会不会显得我很脆弱？","en":"Won't it make me look weak?","note":"显得 xiǎnde = to come across as. 脆弱 cuìruò = fragile.","ex":["问太多问题，","会不会","显得","我","很不专业？"],"exEn":"If I ask too many questions, won't I come across as unprofessional?","id":"会不会显得我很脆弱？","scene":"s18"},{"zh":"是一样的道理。","en":"It's the same principle.","note":"Closes an analogy.","ex":["学语言","和","学游泳","是","一样的道理，","得","多练。"],"exEn":"Learning a language is like learning to swim. Same principle: you have to practise.","id":"是一样的道理。","scene":"s18"},{"zh":"别硬撑。","en":"Don't force yourself to tough it out.","note":"硬撑 = to hold out by sheer will.","ex":["不舒服","就","休息，","千万","别硬撑。"],"exEn":"If you're unwell, rest. Whatever you do, don't push through it.","id":"别硬撑。","scene":"s18"}]},{"id":"s5","line":"L3","zh":"简历怎么改","en":"Fixing the résumé","who":"小雨","setup":"Xiaoyu has applied to more than fifty jobs without a single reply. She brings her résumé.","culture":"海投 (\"casting the net across the sea\") is normal in Chinese campus recruiting, where volume works. Explaining why tailored applications do better in the US reframes the habit without criticising it.","lines":[{"s":"S","zh":"老师，我投了五十多份简历，全都石沉大海了。","en":"I've sent out more than fifty résumés, and every one has vanished without a trace."},{"s":"T","zh":"别灰心，咱们一起看看问题出在哪儿。简历带来了吗？","en":"Don't lose heart. Let's look together at where the problem is. Did you bring your résumé?"},{"s":"S","zh":"带了，您帮我看看。","en":"I did. Please have a look."},{"s":"T","zh":"嗯，内容不少，但是重点不够突出。招聘的人平均只看六七秒。","en":"Hmm. There's plenty here, but the key points don't stand out. Recruiters look for six or seven seconds on average."},{"s":"S","zh":"才六七秒？那我应该怎么改呢？","en":"Only six or seven seconds? Then how should I change it?"},{"s":"T","zh":"第一，把最相关的经历放在最前面；第二，成果尽量用数字说话。","en":"First, put the most relevant experience at the very top. Second, let numbers speak for your results wherever you can."},{"s":"S","zh":"比如说呢？","en":"For example?"},{"s":"T","zh":"比如这句“负责数据分析”，太笼统了。你分析了什么？带来了什么结果？","en":"Take this line, \"responsible for data analysis\". It's too vague. What did you analyse? What result did it bring?"},{"s":"S","zh":"哦，我做的模型帮公司把客户流失率降低了百分之八。","en":"Oh. The model I built helped the company cut customer churn by eight percent."},{"s":"T","zh":"这就对了！把这个写上去，比“负责”两个字有说服力多了。","en":"That's it! Put that in. It's far more convincing than the word \"responsible\"."},{"s":"S","zh":"明白了，我回去就改，改完再发给您看。","en":"Got it. I'll revise it as soon as I get back and send it to you."}],"qs":[{"q":"“石沉大海”在这里是什么意思？","opts":["投了简历却没有任何回音","她去海边玩儿了","她的简历写得很好"],"why":"A stone sinking into the sea: sent off and never heard of again."},{"q":"老师觉得这份简历最大的问题是什么？","opts":["重点不突出，写得太笼统","内容太少","有很多错别字"],"why":"内容不少，但是重点不够突出."}],"chunks":[{"zh":"全都石沉大海了。","en":"They all vanished without a trace.","note":"石沉大海, a stone sinking into the sea, is the stock phrase for applications nobody answers.","ex":["我","发了","三封邮件，","全都","石沉大海了。"],"exEn":"I sent three emails and every one vanished without a trace.","id":"全都石沉大海了。","scene":"s5"},{"zh":"别灰心。","en":"Don't lose heart.","note":"Literally \"don't let your heart turn to ash\".","ex":["被拒了","也","别灰心，","机会","还多着呢。"],"exEn":"Even if you're rejected, don't lose heart. There are plenty more chances.","id":"别灰心。","scene":"s5"},{"zh":"咱们看看问题出在哪儿。","en":"Let's see where the problem is.","note":"咱们 includes the listener, which puts you on the student's side. 出在 = to lie in.","ex":["先","别急着投，","咱们","看看","问题","出在哪儿。"],"exEn":"Don't rush to apply yet. Let's see where the problem is.","id":"咱们看看问题出在哪儿。","scene":"s5"},{"zh":"重点不够突出。","en":"The key points don't stand out enough.","note":"不够 + adjective softens the criticism: not yet enough.","ex":["这份简历","内容","很多，","可是","重点","不够突出。"],"exEn":"This résumé has a lot in it, but the key points don't stand out.","id":"重点不够突出。","scene":"s5"},{"zh":"用数字说话。","en":"Let the numbers do the talking.","note":"Set phrase for \"quantify it\". Also used of analysis in general.","ex":["写成果","的时候，","尽量","用数字","说话。"],"exEn":"When you write up results, let numbers speak as far as you can.","id":"用数字说话。","scene":"s5"},{"zh":"太笼统了。","en":"That's too vague.","note":"笼统 lǒngtǒng = general, sweeping. The cure is 具体, concrete.","ex":["“负责数据分析”","这种说法","太","笼统了。"],"exEn":"\"Responsible for data analysis\" is far too vague a way to put it.","id":"太笼统了。","scene":"s5"},{"zh":"这就对了！","en":"That's it! Now you've got it.","note":"Praise at the moment they get there.","ex":["把","结果","写出来，","这","就","对了！"],"exEn":"Write the result down. That's it!","id":"这就对了！","scene":"s5"}]},{"id":"s6","line":"L3","zh":"内推和人脉","en":"Referrals and reaching out","who":"浩然","setup":"Haoran knows he should network but can't bring himself to message alumni.","culture":"In China opportunity moves through 关系 built over time, so messaging a stranger for help feels presumptuous. Framing a coffee chat as 请教 (asking for guidance) makes it comfortable.","lines":[{"s":"T","zh":"浩然，上次说的那几位校友，你联系了吗？","en":"Haoran, those alumni we talked about last time. Have you contacted them?"},{"s":"S","zh":"还没有……我总觉得麻烦人家不太好。","en":"Not yet… I keep feeling it isn't right to bother them."},{"s":"T","zh":"我理解。不过在美国，找校友聊一聊是很平常的事，算不上麻烦。","en":"I understand. But in the US, having a chat with alumni is perfectly ordinary. It hardly counts as a bother."},{"s":"S","zh":"可是我跟人家又不熟，一上来就求内推，脸皮得多厚啊。","en":"But I don't even know them. Asking for a referral straight off, how thick-skinned would I have to be?"},{"s":"T","zh":"所以别一上来就要内推。先请教一下他们的工作经验，混个脸熟。","en":"So don't ask for a referral straight off. Ask about their work experience first and become a familiar face."},{"s":"S","zh":"那第一封信怎么写比较好？","en":"So how should I write the first message?"},{"s":"T","zh":"简单一点儿：你是谁，为什么对他的工作感兴趣，能不能占用他十五分钟。","en":"Keep it simple: who you are, why his work interests you, and whether you could take fifteen minutes of his time."},{"s":"S","zh":"万一人家不回呢？","en":"What if they don't reply?"},{"s":"T","zh":"不回也很正常，别往心里去。过一个星期再跟进一次就行。","en":"No reply is normal too. Don't take it to heart. Follow up once after a week and that's enough."},{"s":"S","zh":"行，那我今天晚上就试着写一封。","en":"OK. I'll try writing one tonight."},{"s":"T","zh":"写好了发给我，我帮你把把关。","en":"Send it to me when it's done and I'll look it over for you."}],"qs":[{"q":"浩然为什么一直没联系校友？","opts":["他不好意思麻烦不熟的人","他找不到校友的邮箱","他已经找到工作了"],"why":"我总觉得麻烦人家不太好."},{"q":"老师建议第一次联系的时候怎么做？","opts":["先请教工作经验，不要马上求内推","直接请对方内推","先寄一份礼物"],"why":"别一上来就要内推。先请教一下，混个脸熟."}],"chunks":[{"zh":"麻烦人家不太好。","en":"It doesn't feel right to bother them.","note":"人家 = them, said with a respectful distance. Reluctance to 麻烦 people is a real brake on networking.","ex":["我","总觉得","老是","麻烦人家","不太好。"],"exEn":"I keep feeling it isn't right to keep bothering them.","id":"麻烦人家不太好。","scene":"s6"},{"zh":"算不上麻烦。","en":"It hardly counts as a bother.","note":"算不上 = cannot be counted as.","ex":["聊","十五分钟","而已，","根本","算不上","麻烦。"],"exEn":"It's only a fifteen-minute chat. That's no bother at all.","id":"算不上麻烦。","scene":"s6"},{"zh":"能不能帮我内推一下？","en":"Could you put in a referral for me?","note":"内推 = 内部推荐, an employee referral. 一下 keeps the request light.","ex":["有校友","帮忙内推，","简历","就","不容易","石沉大海。"],"exEn":"With an alum referring you, your résumé is less likely to vanish.","id":"能不能帮我内推一下？","scene":"s6"},{"zh":"他脸皮薄。","en":"He's thin-skinned, too shy to ask.","note":"脸皮薄 báo = easily embarrassed. 脸皮厚 = thick-skinned, shameless.","ex":["他","脸皮薄，","不好意思","开口","求人。"],"exEn":"He's thin-skinned and too embarrassed to ask anyone for help.","id":"他脸皮薄。","scene":"s6"},{"zh":"先混个脸熟。","en":"First just become a familiar face.","note":"混 = to get by. 脸熟 = a face people recognise.","ex":["多去","几次","校友活动，","先","混个脸熟。"],"exEn":"Go to a few more alumni events and become a familiar face first.","id":"先混个脸熟。","scene":"s6"},{"zh":"别往心里去。","en":"Don't take it to heart.","note":"往心里去 = let it go to your heart.","ex":["人家","没回信，","你","别","往心里去。"],"exEn":"They didn't write back. Don't take it to heart.","id":"别往心里去。","scene":"s6"},{"zh":"我帮你把把关。","en":"I'll look it over for you.","note":"把关 = to guard the pass. Doubling the verb, 把把关, makes it casual.","ex":["写好了","先","发给我，","我","帮你","把把关。"],"exEn":"Send it to me first when it's written, and I'll check it over.","id":"我帮你把把关。","scene":"s6"}]},{"id":"s7","line":"L3","zh":"留下还是回国","en":"Stay or go home","who":"思琪","setup":"Siqi is torn between job-hunting in the US and going back for autumn recruiting. Her parents have views.","culture":"秋招, autumn campus recruiting (roughly September to November), is the main hiring season in China, with 春招 as the make-up round. Missing it can cost a student their 应届生 (fresh graduate) advantage, which weighs on stay-or-return decisions.","lines":[{"s":"T","zh":"思琪，毕业以后你是想留在美国，还是回国发展？","en":"Siqi, after graduation do you want to stay in the US, or build your career back in China?"},{"s":"S","zh":"我自己想留下来试试，可是身份是个大问题。","en":"I'd like to stay and try, but visa status is a big problem."},{"s":"T","zh":"你们专业算 STEM，OPT 可以延到三年，时间还算宽裕。","en":"Your major counts as STEM, so OPT can be extended to three years. That gives you fair leeway."},{"s":"S","zh":"话是这么说，可是很多公司一听要办工签就不考虑了。","en":"In theory, yes. But a lot of companies stop considering you the moment they hear they would need to sponsor a work visa."},{"s":"T","zh":"确实有这种情况。所以咱们得两手准备，重点投那些愿意办工签的公司。","en":"That does happen. So we need to prepare on both fronts and focus on companies willing to sponsor."},{"s":"S","zh":"我爸妈倒是希望我回去，说女孩子找个稳定的工作就行了。","en":"My parents would actually rather I went back. They say a stable job is enough for a girl."},{"s":"T","zh":"父母的想法可以理解。那你自己心里是怎么想的？","en":"Your parents' view is understandable. And what do you yourself really think?"},{"s":"S","zh":"我想先在这边工作两年，积累点儿经验，回去也更有竞争力。","en":"I'd like to work here for a couple of years first and build up some experience. I'd be more competitive going back, too."},{"s":"T","zh":"这个想法很成熟。国内的秋招你也可以同时关注一下，给自己留条后路。","en":"That's a mature way to think. You could keep an eye on autumn recruiting in China at the same time and leave yourself a way back."},{"s":"S","zh":"嗯，这样我心里就踏实多了。","en":"Mm. That makes me feel a lot more settled."}],"qs":[{"q":"思琪留在美国最担心的是什么？","opts":["身份和工签的问题","找不到房子","英语不够好"],"why":"身份是个大问题."},{"q":"“两手准备”是什么意思？","opts":["同时为两种可能做准备","用两只手写简历","准备两份礼物"],"why":"Two hands, two plans: a plan A and a plan B."},{"q":"父母希望思琪怎么做？","opts":["回国找一份稳定的工作","留在美国","继续读博士"],"why":"我爸妈倒{dào}是希望我回去."}],"chunks":[{"zh":"你是想留在美国，还是回国发展？","en":"Do you want to stay in the US, or build your career back in China?","note":"是…还是… for either/or questions. 发展 = pursue a career.","ex":["毕业以后，","你","是想","留下来，","还是","回国发展？"],"exEn":"After graduation, do you want to stay, or go back to China?","id":"你是想留在美国，还是回国发展？","scene":"s7"},{"zh":"身份是个大问题。","en":"Visa status is a big problem.","note":"身份, literally \"identity\", means immigration status among students abroad. 工签 = work visa. 抽签 = the H-1B lottery.","ex":["对留学生来说，","身份","一直","是个","大问题。"],"exEn":"For international students, status has always been a big problem.","id":"身份是个大问题。","scene":"s7"},{"zh":"话是这么说，可是……","en":"That's true in theory, but…","note":"Concedes the point, then turns. Students use it on you constantly.","ex":["话","是","这么说，","可是","做起来","没那么容易。"],"exEn":"That's true in theory, but doing it isn't so easy.","id":"话是这么说，可是……","scene":"s7"},{"zh":"咱们得两手准备。","en":"We need to prepare for both outcomes.","note":"两手准备 = keep a plan B. 得 děi = must.","ex":["抽签","不一定","抽得中，","所以","得","两手准备。"],"exEn":"You may not win the lottery, so you have to prepare for both.","id":"咱们得两手准备。","scene":"s7"},{"zh":"父母的想法可以理解。","en":"Your parents' view is understandable.","note":"Validate the parents before asking what the student wants.","ex":["父母","希望你","离家近一点儿，","这","也","可以理解。"],"exEn":"Your parents want you closer to home. That is understandable too.","id":"父母的想法可以理解。","scene":"s7"},{"zh":"你自己心里是怎么想的？","en":"What do you yourself really think?","note":"自己 + 心里 separates their own wish from everyone else's.","ex":["先","不管","别人","怎么说，","你自己","是怎么想的？"],"exEn":"Never mind what others say for now. What do you think yourself?","id":"你自己心里是怎么想的？","scene":"s7"},{"zh":"给自己留条后路。","en":"Leave yourself a way back.","note":"后路 = a route of retreat. 留条后路 = keep a fallback.","ex":["多投","几家公司，","也是","给自己","留条后路。"],"exEn":"Applying to a few more companies is also a way of leaving yourself a fallback.","id":"给自己留条后路。","scene":"s7"},{"zh":"心里踏实多了。","en":"I feel a lot more settled.","note":"踏实 tāshi = steady, at ease. Adjective + 多了 = much more.","ex":["有了","备选方案，","心里","就","踏实多了。"],"exEn":"With a backup plan, I feel much more settled.","id":"心里踏实多了。","scene":"s7"}]},{"id":"s8","line":"L4","zh":"模拟面试","en":"Mock interview","who":"子轩","setup":"Zixuan has his first interview on Friday. You run a quick mock.","culture":"Memorising (背) is a strength of Chinese schooling and the default way to prepare for an interview. Redirect it instead of fighting it: memorise the bullet points, not the script.","lines":[{"s":"T","zh":"子轩，周五就要面试了，准备得怎么样了？","en":"Zixuan, the interview's on Friday. How is the preparation going?"},{"s":"S","zh":"自我介绍我背得滚瓜烂熟，可是一紧张脑子就一片空白。","en":"I know my self-introduction backwards. But the moment I get nervous, my mind goes blank."},{"s":"T","zh":"那咱们现在就练一遍。你先说，我来当面试官。","en":"Then let's run through it right now. You start. I'll play the interviewer."},{"s":"S","zh":"好。“我叫王子轩，本科学的是统计，现在在读商业分析硕士……”","en":"OK. \"My name is Wang Zixuan. I studied statistics as an undergraduate and am now doing a master's in business analytics…\""},{"s":"T","zh":"停一下。内容没问题，就是听起来太像背稿子了。","en":"Stop there. The content is fine. It just sounds too much like reciting a script."},{"s":"S","zh":"那怎么才能自然一点儿呢？","en":"So how do I sound more natural?"},{"s":"T","zh":"别逐字逐句地背，记住三个要点就够了，然后用自己的话说出来。","en":"Don't memorise it word for word. Three key points are enough. Then say it in your own words."},{"s":"S","zh":"那行为面试的问题呢？比如“说一次你失败的经历”。","en":"What about behavioural questions? Like \"tell me about a time you failed\"."},{"s":"T","zh":"讲一个具体的故事：当时是什么情况，你做了什么，结果怎么样。","en":"Tell one concrete story: what the situation was, what you did, and how it turned out."},{"s":"S","zh":"明白了，说白了就是要举例子，不能光讲大道理。","en":"Got it. Put plainly, I need to give examples and not just talk in generalities."},{"s":"T","zh":"没错！再来一遍，这次放松一点儿，就当是跟我聊天儿。","en":"Exactly! Once more. Relax a little this time. Just treat it as a chat with me."}],"qs":[{"q":"子轩面试的时候最大的问题是什么？","opts":["一紧张脑子就一片空白","不会说英文","没有准备自我介绍"],"why":"一紧张脑子就一片空白."},{"q":"老师建议怎么准备自我介绍？","opts":["记住几个要点，用自己的话说","逐字逐句背下来","把稿子写在手上"],"why":"记住三个要点就够了{le}，然后用自己的话说出来."}],"chunks":[{"zh":"准备得怎么样了？","en":"How is the preparation going?","note":"Verb + 得 + 怎么样. The final 了 asks for a status update.","ex":["下周的面试，","你","准备得","怎么样了？"],"exEn":"How's the preparation going for next week's interview?","id":"准备得怎么样了？","scene":"s8"},{"zh":"背得滚瓜烂熟。","en":"I've memorised it cold.","note":"滚瓜烂熟: ripe as a melon that rolls off the vine.","ex":["这段话","他","已经","背得","滚瓜烂熟了。"],"exEn":"He already knows this passage backwards.","id":"背得滚瓜烂熟。","scene":"s8"},{"zh":"脑子一片空白。","en":"My mind goes completely blank.","note":"一片 is the measure for an expanse: 一片空白, 一片混乱.","ex":["我","一紧张，","脑子","就","一片空白。"],"exEn":"The moment I get nervous, my mind goes blank.","id":"脑子一片空白。","scene":"s8"},{"zh":"我来当面试官。","en":"I'll play the interviewer.","note":"来 before a verb = let me take this one.","ex":["咱们","练一遍，","这次","我来","当面试官。"],"exEn":"Let's run through it. This time I'll play the interviewer.","id":"我来当面试官。","scene":"s8"},{"zh":"太像背稿子了。","en":"It sounds too much like reciting a script.","note":"稿子 = a draft or script. 背稿子 = recite from memory.","ex":["你说得","很流利，","就是","太像","背稿子了。"],"exEn":"You speak fluently. It just sounds too much like a script.","id":"太像背稿子了。","scene":"s8"},{"zh":"用自己的话说出来。","en":"Say it in your own words.","note":"用…的话 = in …'s words.","ex":["记住","要点，","然后","用自己的话","说出来。"],"exEn":"Remember the key points, then say it in your own words.","id":"用自己的话说出来。","scene":"s8"},{"zh":"说白了，就是要举例子。","en":"Put plainly, you need to give examples.","note":"说白了 = to put it bluntly, in plain terms.","ex":["行为面试，","说白了","就是","讲故事。"],"exEn":"A behavioural interview, put plainly, is storytelling.","id":"说白了，就是要举例子。","scene":"s8"},{"zh":"就当是跟我聊天儿。","en":"Just treat it as a chat with me.","note":"就当(是)… = just think of it as…. 当 is dàng here.","ex":["别紧张，","面试","就当是","跟朋友","聊天儿。"],"exEn":"Don't be nervous. Treat the interview as a chat with a friend.","id":"就当是跟我聊天儿。","scene":"s8"}]},{"id":"s9","line":"L4","zh":"拿到 offer 了","en":"The offer","who":"小雨","setup":"Xiaoyu bursts in with news, then has second thoughts about the salary.","culture":"Many students have never seen anyone negotiate a salary. In a first job in China it is uncommon. 平台 (\"platform\": the employer's name and scale) often counts for more than pay.","lines":[{"s":"S","zh":"老师！我拿到 offer 了！","en":"I got an offer!"},{"s":"T","zh":"真的？太好了，恭喜恭喜！我就知道你没问题。","en":"Really? That's wonderful. Congratulations! I knew you could do it."},{"s":"S","zh":"谢谢老师，多亏您帮我改简历。不过我有点儿纠结。","en":"Thank you. It's all down to your help with my résumé. But I'm a bit torn."},{"s":"T","zh":"纠结什么？说说看。","en":"Torn about what? Tell me."},{"s":"S","zh":"这家公司平台不错，可是薪资比我预期的低了不少。","en":"It's a good company to have on my record, but the salary is a fair bit lower than I expected."},{"s":"T","zh":"薪资是可以谈的。他们给的底薪是多少？有没有签字费？","en":"Salary is negotiable. What base are they offering? Is there a signing bonus?"},{"s":"S","zh":"底薪八万五，没有签字费。我怕一谈，offer 就没了。","en":"Base is eighty-five thousand, no signing bonus. I'm afraid that if I negotiate, the offer will disappear."},{"s":"T","zh":"不会的，只要态度好、有理有据，公司一般不会因为这个收回 offer。","en":"It won't. As long as you're courteous and have good reasons and evidence, companies don't usually withdraw an offer over this."},{"s":"S","zh":"那我应该怎么开口呢？","en":"So how should I bring it up?"},{"s":"T","zh":"先表示感谢，再说你查过市场行情，问他们有没有调整的空间。","en":"Thank them first. Then say you've looked at the market rate, and ask whether there is any room to adjust."},{"s":"S","zh":"好，我试试。要是他们不同意呢？","en":"OK, I'll try. What if they say no?"},{"s":"T","zh":"那也没什么损失。除了钱，发展空间和带你的人也很重要，综合考虑一下。","en":"Then you've lost nothing. Besides money, room to grow and who mentors you matter too. Weigh it all together."}],"qs":[{"q":"小雨为什么纠结？","opts":["薪资比她预期的低","她不喜欢这家公司","公司离家太远"],"why":"薪资比我预期的低了不少."},{"q":"老师觉得谈薪的时候最重要的是什么？","opts":["态度好，而且有理有据","要得越多越好","最好不要谈"],"why":"只要态度好、有理有据."}],"chunks":[{"zh":"恭喜恭喜！我就知道你没问题。","en":"Congratulations! I knew you could do it.","note":"我就知道 = I just knew. Credits them, not luck.","ex":["恭喜恭喜，","我","就知道","你","没问题！"],"exEn":"Congratulations! I knew you would be fine.","id":"恭喜恭喜！我就知道你没问题。","scene":"s9"},{"zh":"多亏你提醒我。","en":"Good thing you reminded me.","note":"多亏 = thanks to, luckily for me.","ex":["多亏","你","提醒我，","不然","我","就忘了。"],"exEn":"Good thing you reminded me, or I'd have forgotten.","id":"多亏你提醒我。","scene":"s9"},{"zh":"我有点儿纠结。","en":"I'm a bit torn.","note":"纠结 jiūjié = tangled up, unable to decide.","ex":["两个 offer","各有好处，","我现在","特别纠结。"],"exEn":"Both offers have their upsides. I'm really torn right now.","id":"我有点儿纠结。","scene":"s9"},{"zh":"薪资是可以谈的。","en":"Salary is negotiable.","note":"是…的 asserts it as a fact. 谈薪 = negotiate pay. 底薪 = base. 签字费 = signing bonus.","ex":["别担心，","薪资","一般","都是","可以谈的。"],"exEn":"Don't worry. Salary is usually negotiable.","id":"薪资是可以谈的。","scene":"s9"},{"zh":"有理有据。","en":"Well reasoned and backed by evidence.","note":"Four characters, two pairs: 有理 (has reason) 有据 (has evidence).","ex":["谈薪的时候，","只要","有理有据，","对方","一般","不会反感。"],"exEn":"When you negotiate, as long as you have reasons and evidence, the other side won't usually mind.","id":"有理有据。","scene":"s9"},{"zh":"有没有调整的空间？","en":"Is there any room to adjust?","note":"The polite, indirect way to ask for more.","ex":["我想问一下，","底薪","还有没有","调整的空间？"],"exEn":"May I ask whether there is still any room to adjust the base?","id":"有没有调整的空间？","scene":"s9"},{"zh":"综合考虑一下。","en":"Weigh everything together.","note":"综合 = taking it all together. 考虑一下 softens it into a suggestion.","ex":["钱","和","发展空间，","你","得","综合考虑","一下。"],"exEn":"Money and room to grow: you have to weigh them together.","id":"综合考虑一下。","scene":"s9"},{"zh":"那也没什么损失。","en":"Then you've lost nothing.","note":"没什么 + noun = not much of any.","ex":["问一下","又","不花钱，","不行","也","没什么损失。"],"exEn":"Asking costs nothing. If it's a no, you've lost nothing.","id":"那也没什么损失。","scene":"s9"}]},{"id":"s10","line":"L4","zh":"被拒了","en":"Turned down","who":"浩然","setup":"Haoran reached a final round and was turned down.","culture":"挂了 (\"hung\") = failed. Blaming 大环境, the wider climate, is a face-saving kindness. 上岸, \"reaching shore\", is how students describe finally landing the job, the exam or the place.","lines":[{"s":"S","zh":"老师，那家公司把我拒了。","en":"That company turned me down."},{"s":"T","zh":"唉，真可惜，都走到终面了。你现在心情怎么样？","en":"Oh, what a shame. You'd got all the way to the final round. How are you feeling?"},{"s":"S","zh":"挺受打击的。我觉得自己什么都不行。","en":"It's a real blow. I feel like I'm no good at anything."},{"s":"T","zh":"先别这么说。能进终面，说明你的实力是被认可的。","en":"Don't say that. Reaching the final round shows your ability was recognised."},{"s":"S","zh":"可是结果还是挂了啊。","en":"But I still failed in the end."},{"s":"T","zh":"这次没成，不代表你不行。今年大环境不好，很多公司都在缩招。","en":"It not working out this time doesn't mean you're not good enough. The climate is bad this year, and many companies are cutting back on hiring."},{"s":"S","zh":"道理我明白，就是心里过不去。","en":"I understand the logic. I just can't get past it."},{"s":"T","zh":"难受是正常的，给自己两天时间缓一缓。然后咱们一起复盘一下。","en":"Feeling bad is normal. Give yourself a couple of days to recover. Then let's go back over it together."},{"s":"S","zh":"复盘？","en":"Go back over it?"},{"s":"T","zh":"对，看看哪些地方答得好，哪些地方还能改进，下次就更有把握了。","en":"Yes. See which parts you answered well and which could be better, so next time you'll be surer of yourself."},{"s":"S","zh":"好。其实有一道案例题我确实没答好。","en":"OK. Actually, there was one case question I really didn't answer well."},{"s":"T","zh":"你看，这就是收获。吃一堑，长一智嘛。","en":"You see, that's something gained already. Live and learn, as they say."}],"qs":[{"q":"老师为什么说浩然的实力是被认可的？","opts":["因为他进了终面","因为他拿到了 offer","因为他成绩很好"],"why":"能进终面，说明你的实力是被认可的."},{"q":"“复盘”是什么意思？","opts":["事后回头分析哪里好、哪里不好","再申请一次","换一家公司"],"why":"From replaying a finished game of Go, move by move."}],"chunks":[{"zh":"真可惜。","en":"What a shame.","note":"Sympathy first, analysis later.","ex":["都","走到","终面了，","没拿到","真可惜。"],"exEn":"You got all the way to the final round. Such a shame it fell through.","id":"真可惜。","scene":"s10"},{"zh":"你现在心情怎么样？","en":"How are you feeling right now?","note":"心情 = mood, state of mind. Asks about the feeling, not the facts.","ex":["发生了","这种事，","你现在","心情","怎么样？"],"exEn":"After something like this, how are you feeling?","id":"你现在心情怎么样？","scene":"s10"},{"zh":"挺受打击的。","en":"It's a real blow.","note":"受打击 = take a hit. 挺…的 = pretty, rather.","ex":["连着","被拒了","三次，","他","挺受打击的。"],"exEn":"Turned down three times in a row. He has taken it hard.","id":"挺受打击的。","scene":"s10"},{"zh":"先别这么说。","en":"Don't say that.","note":"Gently stops the self-criticism. 先 = for now, softening it.","ex":["先","别这么说，","事情","没有","你想的","那么糟。"],"exEn":"Don't say that. Things aren't as bad as you think.","id":"先别这么说。","scene":"s10"},{"zh":"这次没成，不代表你不行。","en":"It not working out this time doesn't mean you're not good enough.","note":"没成 = did not come off. 不代表 = does not mean.","ex":["一次面试","没过，","不代表","你","不行。"],"exEn":"Failing one interview doesn't mean you're not good enough.","id":"这次没成，不代表你不行。","scene":"s10"},{"zh":"今年大环境不好。","en":"The job market is bad this year.","note":"大环境 = the wider climate. 缩招 = cut hiring. 寒冬 = an industry \"winter\".","ex":["今年","大环境","不好，","不是","你一个人","找不到。"],"exEn":"The climate is bad this year. You're not the only one who can't find a job.","id":"今年大环境不好。","scene":"s10"},{"zh":"给自己两天时间缓一缓。","en":"Give yourself a couple of days to recover.","note":"缓一缓 = catch your breath. 两天 = a couple of days, loosely.","ex":["别急，","先","给自己","两天时间","缓一缓。"],"exEn":"No hurry. Give yourself a couple of days to recover first.","id":"给自己两天时间缓一缓。","scene":"s10"},{"zh":"咱们一起复盘一下。","en":"Let's go back over it together.","note":"复盘 fùpán = a post-mortem. Everyday business and student talk.","ex":["每次","面试完，","最好","都","复盘一下。"],"exEn":"After every interview, it's best to go back over it.","id":"咱们一起复盘一下。","scene":"s10"},{"zh":"吃一堑，长一智。","en":"Live and learn.","note":"A fall into the ditch, a gain in wisdom. 长 is zhǎng here.","ex":["这次","没准备好，","下次","就知道了，","吃一堑，","长一智。"],"exEn":"I wasn't prepared this time. Next time I'll know. Live and learn.","id":"吃一堑，长一智。","scene":"s10"}]},{"id":"s11","line":"L5","zh":"讲讲你的项目","en":"Walk me through your project","who":"思琪","setup":"Siqi practises explaining her capstone project to an interviewer who is not technical.","culture":"业务 (the business side) against 技术 (the technical side) is the fault line in every analytics career conversation. 落地, \"landing\", means the analysis was actually put to use.","lines":[{"s":"T","zh":"思琪，给我讲讲你的毕业项目吧，就当我是外行。","en":"Siqi, tell me about your capstone project. Treat me as an outsider."},{"s":"S","zh":"好的。我们帮一家零售公司做了一个预测客户流失的模型。","en":"OK. We built a model for a retail company that predicts customer churn."},{"s":"T","zh":"听起来挺有意思。数据是从哪儿来的？","en":"That sounds interesting. Where did the data come from?"},{"s":"S","zh":"公司给了我们两年的交易数据，不过特别乱，光清洗就花了三个星期。","en":"The company gave us two years of transaction data, but it was a mess. Cleaning alone took three weeks."},{"s":"T","zh":"做分析的都说，八成的时间都花在洗数据上。后来呢？","en":"Analysts all say eighty percent of the time goes on cleaning data. And then?"},{"s":"S","zh":"后来我们试了几种模型，最后选了随机森林，准确率有百分之八十五。","en":"Then we tried several models and settled on a random forest. Accuracy was eighty-five percent."},{"s":"T","zh":"不错。不过面试官可能会问：这个模型对业务到底有什么用？","en":"Good. But the interviewer may ask: what use is this model to the business, really?"},{"s":"S","zh":"嗯……它能提前找出可能流失的客户，这样公司就可以有针对性地发优惠券。","en":"Um… it can pick out customers likely to leave ahead of time, so the company can send coupons in a targeted way."},{"s":"T","zh":"对，这才是重点！先讲业务价值，再讲技术细节。","en":"Yes, that's the real point! Business value first, technical detail second."},{"s":"S","zh":"我一讲起技术就停不下来，老是忘了这一点。","en":"Once I start on the technical side I can't stop. I always forget that."},{"s":"T","zh":"很多人都这样。记住，会做分析是基本功，能把结果讲明白才是本事。","en":"Lots of people do. Remember: doing the analysis is the basic craft. Explaining the result clearly is the real skill."}],"qs":[{"q":"项目里什么事花的时间特别长？","opts":["清洗数据","选模型","写报告"],"why":"光清洗就花了三个星期."},{"q":"老师认为介绍项目的时候应该先讲什么？","opts":["业务价值","技术细节","团队成员"],"why":"先讲业务价值，再讲技术细节."}],"chunks":[{"zh":"就当我是外行。","en":"Treat me as an outsider.","note":"外行 wàiháng = a layperson. Its opposite is 内行.","ex":["你","给我讲的时候，","就当","我","是外行。"],"exEn":"When you explain it to me, treat me as an outsider.","id":"就当我是外行。","scene":"s11"},{"zh":"数据是从哪儿来的？","en":"Where did the data come from?","note":"是…的 puts the focus on where, how or when something already happened.","ex":["这些","交易数据","是","从哪儿","来的？"],"exEn":"Where did this transaction data come from?","id":"数据是从哪儿来的？","scene":"s11"},{"zh":"光清洗就花了三个星期。","en":"Cleaning alone took three weeks.","note":"光…就… = X alone already…","ex":["光","清洗数据","就","花了","三个星期。"],"exEn":"Cleaning the data alone took three weeks.","id":"光清洗就花了三个星期。","scene":"s11"},{"zh":"八成的时间都花在洗数据上。","en":"Eighty percent of the time goes on cleaning data.","note":"八成 = 80%. 花在…上 = spent on.","ex":["分析师","八成的时间","都","花在","洗数据上。"],"exEn":"Eighty percent of an analyst's time goes on cleaning data.","id":"八成的时间都花在洗数据上。","scene":"s11"},{"zh":"对业务到底有什么用？","en":"What use is it to the business, really?","note":"到底 presses for the real answer. 业务 = the business side.","ex":["你的模型","对业务到底","有什么用？"],"exEn":"What use is your model to the business, really?","id":"对业务到底有什么用？","scene":"s11"},{"zh":"有针对性地改简历。","en":"Tailor the résumé to the job.","note":"有针对性 = targeted. With 地 it becomes an adverb.","ex":["每个岗位","都应该","有针对性地","改一下","简历。"],"exEn":"For every role, you should tailor the résumé a little.","id":"有针对性地改简历。","scene":"s11"},{"zh":"这才是重点！","en":"That's the real point!","note":"才 = this and only this.","ex":["能不能","解决问题，","这","才是","重点。"],"exEn":"Whether it solves the problem: that's the real point.","id":"这才是重点！","scene":"s11"},{"zh":"能把结果讲明白才是本事。","en":"Explaining the result clearly is the real skill.","note":"本事 běnshi = real ability. 讲明白 = explain until it is clear.","ex":["会做分析","是基本功，","能把结果","讲明白","才是","本事。"],"exEn":"Doing the analysis is the basic craft. Explaining the result clearly is the real skill.","id":"能把结果讲明白才是本事。","scene":"s11"}]},{"id":"s12","line":"L5","zh":"分析师的一天","en":"A day as an analyst","who":"子轩","setup":"Zixuan can't decide between data analyst and data scientist. You pass on what alumni say.","culture":"取数, \"fetching numbers\", is the self-mocking name for junior analyst work. Nobody wants to be a 取数工具人, a data-pulling tool. Students light up when you know this.","lines":[{"s":"S","zh":"老师，数据分析师和数据科学家到底有什么区别？","en":"What exactly is the difference between a data analyst and a data scientist?"},{"s":"T","zh":"简单来说，分析师更贴近业务，科学家更偏技术和建模。","en":"Simply put, analysts sit closer to the business, and scientists lean towards technology and modelling."},{"s":"S","zh":"那分析师每天都干些什么呢？","en":"So what do analysts actually do all day?"},{"s":"T","zh":"听校友说，主要是取数、做报表、搭看板，还要跟各个部门对接需求。","en":"From what alumni tell me: mostly pulling data, building reports and dashboards, and working through requests with each department."},{"s":"S","zh":"听起来整天都在跑 SQL，会不会很枯燥？","en":"Sounds like running SQL all day. Won't that be dull?"},{"s":"T","zh":"刚入行是这样，免不了的。可是慢慢地，你会从“取数的”变成“出主意的”。","en":"When you're new to the field, yes. It can't be avoided. But little by little you go from the one who pulls the numbers to the one with the ideas."},{"s":"S","zh":"我比较内向，跟业务部门沟通会不会吃亏？","en":"I'm quite introverted. Will I lose out when it comes to dealing with the business teams?"},{"s":"T","zh":"不一定。内向的人往往更会倾听。关键是能把复杂的东西讲成人话。","en":"Not necessarily. Introverts are often better listeners. The key is being able to put complicated things in plain language."},{"s":"S","zh":"“讲人话”，哈哈，这个我得好好练练。","en":"\"Speak human\". Ha, I really need to practise that."},{"s":"T","zh":"对了，你可以多做几个作品集项目，面试的时候拿得出手。","en":"By the way, do a few more portfolio projects, so you have something worth showing in interviews."},{"s":"S","zh":"好主意！那我先从分析师做起，以后再看要不要转方向。","en":"Good idea! I'll start as an analyst and decide later whether to change direction."},{"s":"T","zh":"这样挺稳的，一步一步来。","en":"That's a steady way to go about it. One step at a time."}],"qs":[{"q":"根据老师的说法，分析师和科学家最大的区别是什么？","opts":["分析师更贴近业务，科学家更偏技术","分析师工资更高","科学家不用写代码"],"why":"分析师更贴近业务，科学家更偏技术和建模."},{"q":"老师觉得内向的人有什么优势？","opts":["更会倾听","更会写代码","更喜欢加班"],"why":"内向的人往往更会倾听."}],"chunks":[{"zh":"到底有什么区别？","en":"What exactly is the difference?","note":"到底 = when you get to the bottom of it.","ex":["这两个岗位","到底","有","什么区别？"],"exEn":"What exactly is the difference between these two roles?","id":"到底有什么区别？","scene":"s12"},{"zh":"简单来说，分析师更贴近业务。","en":"Simply put, analysts are closer to the business.","note":"简单来说 = simply put. 贴近 = close up against. 偏 = to lean towards.","ex":["简单来说，","这个岗位","更偏","技术。"],"exEn":"Simply put, this role leans more technical.","id":"简单来说，分析师更贴近业务。","scene":"s12"},{"zh":"跟各个部门对接需求。","en":"Work through requests with each department.","note":"对接 = to interface with. 需求 = requirements. 提需求 = file a request.","ex":["分析师","每天","都要","跟业务部门","对接需求。"],"exEn":"Analysts work through requests with the business teams every day.","id":"跟各个部门对接需求。","scene":"s12"},{"zh":"刚入行是这样，免不了的。","en":"That's how it is when you're new to the field. It can't be avoided.","note":"入行 rùháng = enter a line of work. 免不了 miǎnbuliǎo = unavoidable.","ex":["刚入行","的时候，","加班","是","免不了的。"],"exEn":"When you're new to the field, overtime can't be avoided.","id":"刚入行是这样，免不了的。","scene":"s12"},{"zh":"会不会吃亏？","en":"Will I lose out?","note":"吃亏 = to come off worse. 会不会 = is it likely that.","ex":["不会","写代码，","找工作","会不会","吃亏？"],"exEn":"If I can't code, will I lose out in the job hunt?","id":"会不会吃亏？","scene":"s12"},{"zh":"把复杂的东西讲成人话。","en":"Put complicated things in plain language.","note":"讲人话, \"speak human\", is a playful way to say drop the jargon.","ex":["好的分析师","能把","复杂的结果","讲成","人话。"],"exEn":"A good analyst can put complicated results in plain language.","id":"把复杂的东西讲成人话。","scene":"s12"},{"zh":"面试的时候拿得出手。","en":"Something worth showing in interviews.","note":"拿得出手 = good enough to show.","ex":["多做","几个项目，","面试的时候","才","拿得出手。"],"exEn":"Do a few more projects. Only then will you have something worth showing in interviews.","id":"面试的时候拿得出手。","scene":"s12"},{"zh":"一步一步来。","en":"One step at a time.","note":"Verb-less and calming. Like 慢慢来, with a plan.","ex":["别想","一口吃成胖子，","一步一步","来。"],"exEn":"Don't try to get fat in one bite. One step at a time.","id":"一步一步来。","scene":"s12"}]},{"id":"s17","line":"L4","zh":"实习第一周","en":"First week on the job","who":"子轩","setup":"Zixuan has started his internship and is unsure of the unwritten rules.","culture":"In many Chinese workplaces, leaving before the boss reads as slacking, and interns stay late with nothing to do. 带你的人, \"the one who leads you\", is the informal mentor. 转正 is turning an internship into a full-time offer.","lines":[{"s":"T","zh":"子轩，实习第一周感觉怎么样？","en":"Zixuan, how does the first week of the internship feel?"},{"s":"S","zh":"还在摸索。同事们都挺忙的，我不太敢打扰他们。","en":"I'm still feeling my way. Everyone is busy, and I don't really dare disturb them."},{"s":"T","zh":"刚去都这样。带你的人给你安排活儿了吗？","en":"It's always like that at the start. Has your mentor given you any work?"},{"s":"S","zh":"安排了，让我整理一份竞品分析，可是要求说得很模糊。","en":"Yes. I have to put together a competitor analysis, but the requirements were vague."},{"s":"T","zh":"那你有没有问清楚？","en":"Did you ask for clarification?"},{"s":"S","zh":"没有……我怕问多了显得自己不专业。","en":"No… I was afraid that asking too much would make me look unprofessional."},{"s":"T","zh":"恰恰相反。不懂装懂才最容易出问题，早点儿确认反而显得你靠谱。","en":"Quite the opposite. Pretending to understand is what causes trouble. Checking early makes you look reliable."},{"s":"S","zh":"那怎么问比较合适呢？","en":"So what's a good way to ask?"},{"s":"T","zh":"你可以把自己的理解说一遍，问他“我这样理解对不对”，比直接问“怎么做”好得多。","en":"Say how you understand it, and ask \"am I understanding this right?\" That is far better than asking \"how do I do it?\""},{"s":"S","zh":"这个办法好。还有，下班的时候大家都不走，我也不好意思先走。","en":"That's a good approach. One more thing: at the end of the day nobody leaves, so I feel awkward leaving first."},{"s":"T","zh":"入乡随俗没错，不过活儿干完了就不必硬撑。实习生最重要的是把交给你的事做漂亮。","en":"Following local custom is fine, but once the work is done you needn't sit it out. What matters most for an intern is doing what you're given, and doing it well."},{"s":"S","zh":"嗯，那我先把这份分析做扎实。","en":"Mm. Then I'll make this analysis solid first."},{"s":"T","zh":"对，有什么拿不准的，及时跟你的主管沟通。","en":"Right. And anything you're unsure of, raise it with your supervisor promptly."}],"qs":[{"q":"子轩为什么没有把要求问清楚？","opts":["怕显得自己不专业","主管不在公司","他已经完全明白了"],"why":"我怕问多了显得自己不专业."},{"q":"老师建议怎么提问？","opts":["先说自己的理解，再确认对不对","直接问应该怎么做","最好不要问"],"why":"把自己的理解说一遍，问他“我这样理解对不对”."}],"chunks":[{"zh":"还在摸索。","en":"I'm still feeling my way.","note":"摸索 mōsuo = to grope forward, to work it out as you go.","ex":["这份工作","我","还在","摸索","阶段。"],"exEn":"I'm still at the feeling-my-way stage with this job.","id":"还在摸索。","scene":"s17"},{"zh":"我不敢打扰他们。","en":"I don't dare disturb them.","note":"打扰 = to interrupt or bother. 不敢 = not dare.","ex":["他","看起来","很忙，","我","不敢","打扰他。"],"exEn":"He looks busy. I don't dare bother him.","id":"我不敢打扰他们。","scene":"s17"},{"zh":"要求说得很模糊。","en":"The requirements were vague.","note":"模糊 móhu = blurry, unclear.","ex":["领导的要求","说得","很模糊，","我","不知道","从哪儿下手。"],"exEn":"The boss's requirements were vague. I don't know where to start.","id":"要求说得很模糊。","scene":"s17"},{"zh":"恰恰相反。","en":"Quite the opposite.","note":"恰恰 = exactly, precisely.","ex":["我以为","他会生气，","结果","恰恰相反。"],"exEn":"I thought he would be angry. It turned out quite the opposite.","id":"恰恰相反。","scene":"s17"},{"zh":"不懂装懂最容易出问题。","en":"Pretending to understand is what causes trouble.","note":"不懂装懂 = not understand yet act as if you do.","ex":["不懂","就问，","千万","别","不懂装懂。"],"exEn":"If you don't understand, ask. Never pretend you do.","id":"不懂装懂最容易出问题。","scene":"s17"},{"zh":"我这样理解对不对？","en":"Am I understanding this right?","note":"Shows your thinking and asks for a check in one move.","ex":["您的意思","是","先做北美市场，","我这样理解","对不对？"],"exEn":"You mean do the North American market first. Am I understanding that right?","id":"我这样理解对不对？","scene":"s17"},{"zh":"把交给你的事做漂亮。","en":"Do what you're given, and do it well.","note":"做漂亮 = make a fine job of it.","ex":["先","把","手头的事","做漂亮，","再","考虑别的。"],"exEn":"First do the work in hand well. Then think about other things.","id":"把交给你的事做漂亮。","scene":"s17"},{"zh":"有什么拿不准的，及时沟通。","en":"Anything you're unsure of, raise it promptly.","note":"拿不准 = cannot be sure. 及时 = in good time.","ex":["有","拿不准的地方，","要","及时","跟主管沟通。"],"exEn":"Wherever you're unsure, talk to your supervisor promptly.","id":"有什么拿不准的，及时沟通。","scene":"s17"}]},{"id":"s15","line":"L5","zh":"用数据讲故事","en":"Presenting to the boss","who":"小雨","setup":"Xiaoyu, now an intern, has to present her dashboard to a manager who is not technical.","culture":"汇报, reporting upwards, is a core workplace ritual, and 领导 (\"the leader\") is what staff call any boss. Juniors are expected to be thorough. \"Conclusion first\" runs against the school habit of building up to the point.","lines":[{"s":"S","zh":"老师，下周我要给部门领导做汇报，有点儿发怵。","en":"Next week I have to present to the head of the department, and I'm a bit daunted."},{"s":"T","zh":"第一次给领导汇报都会紧张。你打算讲什么？","en":"Everyone is nervous the first time. What do you plan to cover?"},{"s":"S","zh":"我做了一个销售看板，想把所有的指标都展示一遍。","en":"I built a sales dashboard, and I want to go through every metric."},{"s":"T","zh":"所有的？领导的时间有限，你得先想清楚：他最关心的是什么？","en":"Every one? A manager's time is limited. First work out what he cares about most."},{"s":"S","zh":"应该是……为什么上个季度的销售额下滑了。","en":"Probably… why sales slipped last quarter."},{"s":"T","zh":"那就开门见山，先说结论，再用两三张图来支撑。","en":"Then get straight to the point. Conclusion first, then two or three charts to back it up."},{"s":"S","zh":"可是我辛辛苦苦做了二十多张图，不讲岂不是白做了？","en":"But I slaved over more than twenty charts. If I don't show them, wasn't it all for nothing?"},{"s":"T","zh":"不会白做，放在附录里，有人问到再拿出来。图不在多，在于能不能说明问题。","en":"Not for nothing. Put them in an appendix and bring them out if someone asks. It isn't how many charts. It's whether they make the point."},{"s":"S","zh":"也是。那结论应该怎么说才有说服力？","en":"True. So how should I put the conclusion to make it convincing?"},{"s":"T","zh":"别只说“销售额下降了百分之十二”，要说清楚原因是什么，接下来建议怎么做。","en":"Don't only say \"sales fell twelve percent\". Say what caused it, and what you recommend next."},{"s":"S","zh":"明白了，就是从“发生了什么”讲到“为什么”，再讲到“怎么办”。","en":"I see. From \"what happened\" to \"why\", and then to \"what to do\"."},{"s":"T","zh":"总结得很到位！讲之前找个同事预演一遍，心里就有底了。","en":"That sums it up exactly! Rehearse once with a colleague beforehand and you'll feel sure of yourself."}],"qs":[{"q":"领导最关心的是什么？","opts":["上个季度的销售额为什么下滑","看板做得好不好看","小雨一共做了多少张图"],"why":"为什么上个季度的销售额下滑了."},{"q":"老师建议怎么安排这次汇报？","opts":["先说结论，再用几张图来支撑","把二十多张图都讲一遍","先讲技术细节"],"why":"开门见山，先说结论，再用两三张图来支撑."}],"chunks":[{"zh":"我有点儿发怵。","en":"I'm a bit daunted.","note":"发怵 fāchù = dread before a task. Colloquial, northern in flavour.","ex":["一想到","要上台","讲话，","我","就","发怵。"],"exEn":"The moment I think of getting up to speak, I feel daunted.","id":"我有点儿发怵。","scene":"s15"},{"zh":"开门见山。","en":"Get straight to the point.","note":"Open the door and there is the mountain.","ex":["时间不多，","咱们","就","开门见山","吧。"],"exEn":"There isn't much time, so let's get straight to the point.","id":"开门见山。","scene":"s15"},{"zh":"先说结论，再用数据来支撑。","en":"Conclusion first, then back it up with data.","note":"结论 = conclusion. 支撑 zhīchēng = to prop up, support.","ex":["汇报的时候，","先说结论，","再","用数据","来支撑。"],"exEn":"When you present, give the conclusion first, then back it up with data.","id":"先说结论，再用数据来支撑。","scene":"s15"},{"zh":"岂不是白做了？","en":"Wouldn't that all be for nothing?","note":"岂不是 = wouldn't that be (rhetorical). 白 + verb = in vain.","ex":["这么多图","都不讲，","岂不是","白做了？"],"exEn":"If I show none of these charts, wasn't making them a waste?","id":"岂不是白做了？","scene":"s15"},{"zh":"图不在多，在于能不能说明问题。","en":"It isn't how many charts. It's whether they make the point.","note":"不在…在于… = it lies not in X but in Y.","ex":["简历","不在长，","在于","有没有","亮点。"],"exEn":"A résumé isn't about length. It's about whether it has highlights.","id":"图不在多，在于能不能说明问题。","scene":"s15"},{"zh":"销售额下滑了。","en":"Sales have slipped.","note":"销售额 = sales revenue. 下滑 = to slide. 季度 = quarter.","ex":["上个季度的","销售额","下滑了","百分之十二。"],"exEn":"Last quarter's sales slipped twelve percent.","id":"销售额下滑了。","scene":"s15"},{"zh":"总结得很到位。","en":"That sums it up exactly.","note":"到位 = right on the mark.","ex":["你这个分析","做得","很到位，","领导","一定满意。"],"exEn":"Your analysis is right on the mark. The boss is sure to be pleased.","id":"总结得很到位。","scene":"s15"},{"zh":"心里就有底了。","en":"Then you'll feel sure of yourself.","note":"有底 = to know where you stand.","ex":["多练","几遍，","上台的时候","心里","就有底了。"],"exEn":"Practise a few more times, and you'll feel sure of yourself on stage.","id":"心里就有底了。","scene":"s15"}]},{"id":"s16","line":"L5","zh":"AI 会不会抢饭碗","en":"Will AI take the job?","who":"浩然","setup":"Haoran worries that analysts are about to be replaced by AI.","culture":"大模型 (\"large model\") is the everyday word for an LLM, and 提示词 is a prompt. 抢饭碗, \"snatching the rice bowl\", is how losing work to anyone or anything is described. The worry about entry-level analyst jobs is real in this cohort.","lines":[{"s":"S","zh":"老师，现在大模型这么厉害，写代码、做图表都会，分析师会不会被取代啊？","en":"Large models are so capable now. They write code, they make charts. Are analysts going to be replaced?"},{"s":"T","zh":"这个问题最近好多同学都在问。你自己平时用得多吗？","en":"A lot of students have been asking that lately. Do you use them much yourself?"},{"s":"S","zh":"天天用，写 SQL 基本上靠它，效率确实高了不少。","en":"Every day. I basically rely on one for SQL. It really has made me a good deal more efficient."},{"s":"T","zh":"那你觉得它哪些地方还不行？","en":"And where do you think it still falls short?"},{"s":"S","zh":"它不了解业务背景，有时候一本正经地胡说八道，还得我自己核对。","en":"It doesn't know the business background. Sometimes it talks complete nonsense with a straight face, and I still have to check it myself."},{"s":"T","zh":"这就是关键。工具越强，越需要有人判断结果靠不靠谱、问对问题。","en":"That's the key. The stronger the tool, the more you need someone to judge whether the result is reliable, and to ask the right question."},{"s":"S","zh":"所以说，被取代的不是分析师，而是不会用 AI 的分析师？","en":"So the ones who get replaced aren't analysts, but analysts who can't use AI?"},{"s":"T","zh":"可以这么理解。与其担心，不如把它当成帮手，把省下来的时间花在理解业务上。","en":"You could put it that way. Rather than worry, treat it as a helper, and spend the time you save on understanding the business."},{"s":"S","zh":"那面试的时候，要不要主动提自己会用这些工具？","en":"In interviews, should I bring up that I can use these tools?"},{"s":"T","zh":"当然要提，但别只说“我会用”，要举例说明你是怎么用它解决实际问题的。","en":"Certainly. But don't only say \"I can use it\". Give an example of how you used it to solve a real problem."},{"s":"S","zh":"有道理，我回去好好整理一下。","en":"That makes sense. I'll go and put that together properly."},{"s":"T","zh":"技术更新换代很快，保持好奇心比什么都重要。","en":"The technology turns over fast. Staying curious matters more than anything."}],"qs":[{"q":"浩然觉得大模型有什么问题？","opts":["不了解业务背景，有时候会胡说","写代码太慢","用起来太贵"],"why":"它不了解业务背景，有时候一本正经地胡说八道."},{"q":"老师的态度是什么？","opts":["把 AI 当成帮手，多花时间理解业务","最好不要用 AI","分析师一定会被取代"],"why":"与其担心，不如把它当成帮手."}],"chunks":[{"zh":"分析师会不会被取代？","en":"Will analysts be replaced?","note":"取代 = to take the place of. With 被 it is passive.","ex":["很多人","担心","自己的工作","会被","AI","取代。"],"exEn":"Many people worry that their job will be replaced by AI.","id":"分析师会不会被取代？","scene":"s16"},{"zh":"效率高了不少。","en":"It's made me a good deal more efficient.","note":"效率 = efficiency. Adjective + 了不少 = a good deal more.","ex":["用了","新工具","以后，","效率","高了不少。"],"exEn":"Since I started using the new tool, I am a good deal more efficient.","id":"效率高了不少。","scene":"s16"},{"zh":"一本正经地胡说八道。","en":"Talking complete nonsense with a straight face.","note":"The standing joke about AI making things up. 一本正经 = dead serious. 胡说八道 = to talk rubbish.","ex":["它","有时候","一本正经地","胡说八道。"],"exEn":"Sometimes it talks complete nonsense with a straight face.","id":"一本正经地胡说八道。","scene":"s16"},{"zh":"还得我自己核对。","en":"I still have to check it myself.","note":"核对 héduì = to verify against the source.","ex":["结果","出来以后，","还得","自己","核对一遍。"],"exEn":"Once the results are out, you still have to check them yourself.","id":"还得我自己核对。","scene":"s16"},{"zh":"靠不靠谱？","en":"Is it reliable?","note":"靠谱 kàopǔ = dependable, of people and of data.","ex":["这个数据来源","到底","靠不靠谱？"],"exEn":"Is this data source actually reliable?","id":"靠不靠谱？","scene":"s16"},{"zh":"可以这么理解。","en":"You could put it that way.","note":"Accepts someone's summary without fully owning it.","ex":["可以","这么理解，","但是","情况","没那么简单。"],"exEn":"You could put it that way, but the situation isn't that simple.","id":"可以这么理解。","scene":"s16"},{"zh":"与其担心，不如把它当成帮手。","en":"Rather than worry, treat it as a helper.","note":"与其 A，不如 B = rather than A, better B.","ex":["与其","在家里着急，","不如","出去","走走。"],"exEn":"Rather than fret at home, better to go out for a walk.","id":"与其担心，不如把它当成帮手。","scene":"s16"},{"zh":"技术更新换代很快。","en":"The technology turns over fast.","note":"更新换代 gēngxīn huàndài = one generation replacing the last.","ex":["这个行业","更新换代","太快，","得","不断学习。"],"exEn":"This industry turns over so fast that you have to keep learning.","id":"技术更新换代很快。","scene":"s16"}]}];
export const CHENGYU = [{"zh":"脱颖而出","en":"to stand out from the crowd","lit":"the awl point pokes out of the bag","clue":"几百份简历里，只有亮点突出的才能＿＿＿＿。","clueEn":"Out of hundreds of résumés, only the ones with clear highlights ___.","id":"y:脱颖而出"},{"zh":"胸有成竹","en":"to have it all worked out in advance","lit":"a finished bamboo already in the chest","clue":"她准备得很充分，走进面试室的时候＿＿＿＿。","clueEn":"She had prepared thoroughly and walked into the interview room ___.","id":"y:胸有成竹"},{"zh":"半途而废","en":"to give up halfway","lit":"abandon it mid-road","clue":"学编程最怕＿＿＿＿，坚持三个月就不一样了。","clueEn":"The worst thing in learning to code is ___. Stick at it for three months and things change.","id":"y:半途而废"},{"zh":"循序渐进","en":"step by step, in proper order","lit":"follow the sequence, advance gradually","clue":"学语言不能着急，得＿＿＿＿。","clueEn":"You can't rush a language. It has to be ___.","id":"y:循序渐进"},{"zh":"一举两得","en":"to kill two birds with one stone","lit":"one move, two gains","clue":"边实习边做毕业项目，真是＿＿＿＿。","clueEn":"Doing the capstone project during the internship really is ___.","id":"y:一举两得"},{"zh":"扬长避短","en":"to play to your strengths","lit":"raise the long, avoid the short","clue":"面试的时候要＿＿＿＿，多讲自己最拿手的。","clueEn":"In an interview you should ___ and talk about what you do best.","id":"y:扬长避短"},{"zh":"实事求是","en":"to stick to the facts","lit":"seek truth from facts","clue":"简历上的数字一定要＿＿＿＿，不能夸大。","clueEn":"The numbers on a résumé must ___. No exaggerating.","id":"y:实事求是"},{"zh":"纸上谈兵","en":"all theory, no practice","lit":"discussing war on paper","clue":"只上课不实习，说得再好也是＿＿＿＿。","clueEn":"Classes without internships: however well you talk, it is ___.","id":"y:纸上谈兵"},{"zh":"眼高手低","en":"high standards, modest ability","lit":"eyes high, hands low","clue":"刚毕业就非大公司不去，小心别人说你＿＿＿＿。","clueEn":"Fresh out of school and only big companies will do? Careful, or people will call you ___.","id":"y:眼高手低"},{"zh":"熟能生巧","en":"practice makes perfect","lit":"familiarity gives birth to skill","clue":"面试没有捷径，多练几次，＿＿＿＿。","clueEn":"There is no shortcut for interviews. Practise a few more times: ___.","id":"y:熟能生巧"},{"zh":"举一反三","en":"to learn one thing and apply it to others","lit":"raise one, infer three","clue":"好的分析师学会一个方法，就能＿＿＿＿。","clueEn":"A good analyst learns one method and can ___.","id":"y:举一反三"},{"zh":"一目了然","en":"clear at a glance","lit":"one look and it is understood","clue":"好的图表应该让人＿＿＿＿。","clueEn":"A good chart should be ___.","id":"y:一目了然"},{"zh":"言简意赅","en":"brief and to the point","lit":"words few, meaning complete","clue":"自我介绍别太长，要＿＿＿＿。","clueEn":"Don't make the self-introduction too long. It should be ___.","id":"y:言简意赅"},{"zh":"对症下药","en":"to fit the remedy to the problem","lit":"prescribe for the symptom","clue":"先弄清楚简历的问题在哪儿，才能＿＿＿＿。","clueEn":"Work out where the résumé goes wrong first. Only then can you ___.","id":"y:对症下药"},{"zh":"一针见血","en":"to go straight to the heart of it","lit":"one needle prick draws blood","clue":"面试官的问题＿＿＿＿，一下子就问到了项目的弱点。","clueEn":"The interviewer's question ___ and went straight to the project's weak spot.","id":"y:一针见血"},{"zh":"患得患失","en":"to fret over every gain and loss","lit":"worry about getting, worry about losing","clue":"等 offer 的那几天，他＿＿＿＿，觉都睡不好。","clueEn":"In the days he waited for the offer, he ___ and could not even sleep.","id":"y:患得患失"},{"zh":"急于求成","en":"impatient for quick results","lit":"anxious to seek success","clue":"找工作不能＿＿＿＿，得一步一步来。","clueEn":"In a job hunt you can't be ___. Take it step by step.","id":"y:急于求成"},{"zh":"水到渠成","en":"things fall into place when the time is ripe","lit":"where water flows, a channel forms","clue":"平时多积累，机会来了自然＿＿＿＿。","clueEn":"Keep building up day to day, and when the chance comes, ___.","id":"y:水到渠成"},{"zh":"未雨绸缪","en":"to prepare before trouble comes","lit":"bind the windows before it rains","clue":"签证的事要＿＿＿＿，别等到最后一刻。","clueEn":"With visas you must ___. Don't leave it to the last minute.","id":"y:未雨绸缪"},{"zh":"入乡随俗","en":"when in Rome, do as the Romans do","lit":"enter the village, follow its customs","clue":"到了美国，面试以后发感谢信，算是＿＿＿＿吧。","clueEn":"In America you send a thank-you note after an interview. Call it ___.","id":"y:入乡随俗"},{"zh":"顺其自然","en":"to let things take their course","lit":"follow its nature","clue":"该做的都做了，结果就＿＿＿＿吧。","clueEn":"You've done all you should. As for the result, ___.","id":"y:顺其自然"},{"zh":"再接再厉","en":"keep it up, push on","lit":"whet the beak again before each bout","clue":"这次面试表现不错，下次＿＿＿＿！","clueEn":"You did well in this interview. Next time, ___!","id":"y:再接再厉"},{"zh":"精益求精","en":"to keep refining what is already good","lit":"from fine, seek finer","clue":"简历已经不错了，可是她还在＿＿＿＿，改了第十遍。","clueEn":"The résumé was already good, but she was still ___, on her tenth revision.","id":"y:精益求精"},{"zh":"随机应变","en":"to think on your feet","lit":"follow the moment, respond to change","clue":"面试官的问题不可能都猜到，要学会＿＿＿＿。","clueEn":"You can't guess every question an interviewer will ask. Learn to ___.","id":"y:随机应变"},{"zh":"临阵磨枪","en":"to cram at the last minute","lit":"sharpen the spear just before battle","clue":"明天就面试了，今天才开始准备，真是＿＿＿＿。","clueEn":"The interview is tomorrow and you start preparing today. That really is ___.","id":"y:临阵磨枪"},{"zh":"独当一面","en":"able to take charge on your own","lit":"hold one front alone","clue":"工作两三年以后，她已经能＿＿＿＿了。","clueEn":"After two or three years on the job, she could already ___.","id":"y:独当一面"},{"zh":"大材小用","en":"talent wasted on a small job","lit":"big timber, small use","clue":"让一个博士天天做报表，有点儿＿＿＿＿了。","clueEn":"Having a PhD make reports every day is a bit ___.","id":"y:大材小用"},{"zh":"好高骛远","en":"to reach for what is far beyond you","lit":"love the high, chase the far","clue":"先把基础打好，别＿＿＿＿。","clueEn":"Get the foundations right first. Don't ___.","id":"y:好高骛远"},{"zh":"各有千秋","en":"each has its own merits","lit":"each has a thousand autumns","clue":"这两个 offer ＿＿＿＿，很难说哪个更好。","clueEn":"These two offers ___. It is hard to say which is better.","id":"y:各有千秋"},{"zh":"集思广益","en":"to pool ideas for a better result","lit":"gather thoughts, widen benefit","clue":"小组讨论的好处就是能＿＿＿＿。","clueEn":"The good thing about group discussion is that you can ___.","id":"y:集思广益"},{"zh":"滥竽充数","en":"to fill a seat without the skill","lit":"a fake player padding out the pipe band","clue":"小组里总有人不干活儿，＿＿＿＿。","clueEn":"There is always someone in the group who does no work, just ___.","id":"y:滥竽充数"},{"zh":"雪中送炭","en":"help when it is needed most","lit":"send charcoal in the snow","clue":"我最难的时候您帮我内推，真是＿＿＿＿。","clueEn":"You referred me at my hardest moment. That truly was ___.","id":"y:雪中送炭"},{"zh":"自相矛盾","en":"to contradict yourself","lit":"your own spear against your own shield","clue":"你先说喜欢团队合作，后来又说喜欢一个人干，有点儿＿＿＿＿。","clueEn":"First you say you like teamwork, then that you like working alone. That is a bit ___.","id":"y:自相矛盾"},{"zh":"脚踏实地","en":"down to earth, steady","lit":"feet treading solid ground","clue":"不管在哪家公司，都要＿＿＿＿地做事。","clueEn":"Whichever company you are at, do the work in a ___ way.","id":"y:脚踏实地"},{"zh":"塞翁失马","en":"a blessing in disguise","lit":"the old man at the frontier loses his horse","clue":"没去成那家公司，后来拿到了更好的 offer，真是＿＿＿＿。","clueEn":"He didn't get into that company and later landed a better offer. Truly ___.","id":"y:塞翁失马"}];
export const REGISTER = [{"id":"r1","sit":"A student thanks you again and again after an hour on their résumé. Wave it off warmly.","opts":[{"zh":"别客气，这是我应该做的。","fb":"Warm and modest. \"It is what I should do\" is the classic gracious reply."},{"zh":"不用谢，这是我的工作。","fb":"Correct but cool. \"It is my job\" sounds transactional."},{"zh":"没关系。","fb":"没关系 answers an apology, not thanks."}]},{"id":"r2","sit":"A student says: 您中文说得真好！ What is the natural reply?","opts":[{"zh":"哪里哪里，还差得远呢。","fb":"Deflect first. After that you can chat about where you learned."},{"zh":"谢谢，我知道。","fb":"Taking the praise, and adding \"I know\", sounds arrogant."},{"zh":"是的，我学了很多年。","fb":"Grammatical, but agreeing with a compliment sounds boastful."}]},{"id":"r3","sit":"The résumé needs major rework. Say so without crushing the student.","opts":[{"zh":"整体不错，不过有几个地方可以再调整一下。","fb":"Praise, then \"a few places could be adjusted\", softened by 可以 and 一下. This is how face is kept."},{"zh":"你的简历问题很多，要重写。","fb":"Possibly accurate, and blunt enough to make a student shut down."},{"zh":"这份简历不行。","fb":"A flat verdict. Too harsh from a 老师 they trust."}]},{"id":"r4","sit":"You meet a student's visiting mother for the first time.","opts":[{"zh":"您好，很高兴认识您。","fb":"您 is expected with parents and elders."},{"zh":"你好啊，最近怎么样？","fb":"Too casual for a first meeting with a parent."},{"zh":"久仰大名。","fb":"\"I have long admired your great name.\" For dignitaries. Comically grand here."}]},{"id":"r5","sit":"A student says 我考砸了 (I bombed the exam). Comfort first.","opts":[{"zh":"没事儿，一次考试说明不了什么。","fb":"Shrinks the stakes: one exam proves nothing."},{"zh":"你应该早点儿复习。","fb":"Advice that lands as blame. True, and no help right now."},{"zh":"加油！","fb":"加油 cheers someone on before or during an effort. On its own after a failure it can feel dismissive."}]},{"id":"r6","sit":"A student invites you to dinner. You have to decline.","opts":[{"zh":"谢谢你的好意，我心领了，不过这周实在抽不出时间。","fb":"心领了, \"my heart accepts it\", declines the meal while honouring the gesture."},{"zh":"不行，我不能去。","fb":"Clear but abrupt. A bare refusal costs the student face."},{"zh":"我不想去。","fb":"\"I do not want to.\" Honest, and wounding."}]},{"id":"r7","sit":"A student is late for the third time. Flag it firmly but kindly.","opts":[{"zh":"下次尽量准时，好吗？面试迟到可就麻烦了。","fb":"A request, a 好吗, and a reason tied to their own interest."},{"zh":"你怎么又迟到了？","fb":"怎么又… is how a parent scolds a child."},{"zh":"迟到是不对的。","fb":"Sounds like a moral lecture."}]},{"id":"r8","sit":"A student asks: 老师，您能保证我找到工作吗？","opts":[{"zh":"保证不了，但是我会尽力帮你。","fb":"An honest \"cannot guarantee\" followed by a commitment."},{"zh":"没问题，包在我身上。","fb":"\"Leave it to me!\" A promise you cannot keep."},{"zh":"这不是我的责任。","fb":"True, and cold."}]},{"id":"r9","sit":"A student applies only to the most famous firms. Suggest widening the search.","opts":[{"zh":"要不要也考虑一下中小公司？机会可能更多。","fb":"要不要…？ floats the idea as a question, so the decision stays theirs."},{"zh":"你必须投小公司。","fb":"必须 is an order."},{"zh":"你太眼高手低了。","fb":"Name-calling by idiom."}]},{"id":"r10","sit":"The session is ending. Make the student feel welcome to come back.","opts":[{"zh":"有什么问题随时来找我。","fb":"随时, \"anytime\", is the open door."},{"zh":"再见，下一个。","fb":"Sounds like an assembly line."},{"zh":"你可以走了。","fb":"\"You may go.\" A dismissal."}]},{"id":"r11","sit":"A student lands an offer. Give the credit to their effort.","opts":[{"zh":"这都是你自己努力的结果。","fb":"Crediting effort is the highest compliment."},{"zh":"你运气真好！","fb":"\"So lucky!\" undercuts the work they put in."},{"zh":"我早就告诉过你了。","fb":"\"I told you so\" makes it about you."}]},{"id":"r12","sit":"You have forgotten a returning student's name.","opts":[{"zh":"不好意思，你的名字我一下子想不起来了。","fb":"Own the lapse. 一下子想不起来 = it has slipped my mind for a moment."},{"zh":"你叫什么？","fb":"Fine for a stranger. Too bare for someone you have met."},{"zh":"您贵姓？","fb":"Over-formal for a student. 您贵姓 points up the hierarchy, not down."}]},{"id":"r13","sit":"You disagree with a plan to quit an internship early. Open gently.","opts":[{"zh":"我理解你的想法，不过我有点儿不同的看法。","fb":"Acknowledge, then 不过 with a 有点儿 softener."},{"zh":"你错了。","fb":"Direct contradiction costs face."},{"zh":"这个想法太傻了。","fb":"An insult."}]},{"id":"r14","sit":"A student messages you on WeChat: 老师在吗？ Reply in a friendly texting voice.","opts":[{"zh":"在的，怎么啦？","fb":"在的 and 怎么啦: soft final particles are what friendly texting sounds like."},{"zh":"我在。请问有何贵干？","fb":"有何贵干 is stiff and classical, and can read as sarcastic."},{"zh":"什么事？","fb":"Curt. Reads as annoyed in a text."}]},{"id":"r15","sit":"A student brings you tea from home. Accept graciously.","opts":[{"zh":"哎呀，太客气了，还特地带东西来。","fb":"A mild protest first (\"you are too polite!\") is the expected ritual before accepting."},{"zh":"谢谢，我正好需要。","fb":"Accepting eagerly skips the ritual and sounds a little greedy."},{"zh":"我不能收。","fb":"A flat refusal makes the giver lose face. If policy says no, soften it."}]},{"id":"r16","sit":"A nervous student apologises for their English before a mock interview.","opts":[{"zh":"你的英文已经很不错了，放松点儿。","fb":"Specific reassurance, then permission to relax."},{"zh":"没关系，反正大家都听得懂。","fb":"反正, \"anyway\", implies it is bad but tolerable."},{"zh":"你确实需要多练。","fb":"Honest, and the opposite of reassuring."}]},{"id":"r17","sit":"You want to ask how a student's family sees their plans. It may be sensitive.","opts":[{"zh":"方便问一下吗？你家里人是怎么看这件事的？","fb":"方便问一下吗, \"may I ask?\", gives them a way out."},{"zh":"告诉我你父母的想法。","fb":"A command."},{"zh":"你父母同意吗？","fb":"A yes-or-no question about approval puts them on the spot."}]},{"id":"r18","sit":"A student asks for a recommendation letter you are glad to write.","opts":[{"zh":"没问题，包在我身上。","fb":"Here 包在我身上 fits, because the thing is fully in your power."},{"zh":"可以考虑。","fb":"\"I can consider it\" usually signals a polite no."},{"zh":"好吧。","fb":"好吧 is a reluctant OK."}]}];
export const TALKS = [{"id":"smalltalk","zh":"随便聊聊","en":"Small talk","brief":"A first-year drops by your office with nothing urgent.","role":"You are 小雨, a first-year business analytics master's student from Chengdu, dropping by the career advisor's office to say hello. You are friendly and a little shy. Things you might bring up: missing hotpot, a trip last weekend, a class you find hard, the weather compared with home."},{"id":"resume","zh":"改简历","en":"Résumé review","brief":"His bullet points are vague. Help him find what he actually did.","role":"You are 浩然, a second-year master's student from Suzhou. Your résumé is vague (\"负责数据分析\") and you have sent fifty applications with no reply. You did one internship at a bank in Suzhou, where you built a churn model that cut customer loss by 8 percent, but you only mention this if the advisor asks what you actually did. You are a little defensive at first, then open up."},{"id":"mock","zh":"模拟面试","en":"Mock interview","brief":"You are the interviewer. Ask, listen, then tell him how it went.","role":"You are 子轩, a nervous master's student in a mock interview. The advisor plays the interviewer. Your answers sound memorised and run slightly long, and you forget to give concrete examples unless pushed. After three or four questions, ask how you did and what to fix."},{"id":"rejected","zh":"被拒之后","en":"After a rejection","brief":"She reached the final round and was turned down this morning.","role":"You are 思琪, a master's student who was rejected this morning after a final-round interview at a company you really wanted. You are discouraged and blame yourself (\"我觉得自己什么都不行\"). You brighten gradually if the advisor listens before giving advice."},{"id":"offer","zh":"要不要谈薪","en":"Negotiating an offer","brief":"An offer has arrived and she is afraid to ask for more.","role":"You are 小雨. You have an offer from a mid-size retailer in Chicago: base salary 82,000 dollars, no signing bonus, reply due Friday. You are also waiting to hear from a second company. You are afraid that negotiating will make the offer disappear, and you have never negotiated anything."},{"id":"stay","zh":"留下还是回国","en":"Stay or go home","brief":"OPT, parents, a girlfriend, and no easy answer.","role":"You are 浩然. You are torn between job-hunting in the US on OPT and going home. Your parents in Suzhou want you back to sit the civil-service exam (考公). Your girlfriend is staying in the US. You worry about the H-1B lottery. You want to think aloud, not be told what to do."},{"id":"network","zh":"不敢联系校友","en":"Reaching out to alumni","brief":"She knows she should message alumni and has not sent one.","role":"You are 思琪. The advisor suggested three alumni to contact two weeks ago and you have messaged none of them. You feel it would be 麻烦人家 and do not know what to write. If the advisor helps, you try drafting a first message aloud and ask whether it sounds right."},{"id":"parent","zh":"见家长","en":"Meeting a parent","brief":"A visiting mother has questions. Use 您.","role":"You are 王阿姨, mother of the student 子轩, visiting from Nanjing. You are polite and a little formal, and you address the advisor as 老师 and 您. You are worried about the American job market, wonder whether your son should come home, and want to know honestly how he is doing. You thank the advisor warmly and may offer a small gift of tea."},{"id":"alum","zh":"请教校友","en":"Ask an alum","brief":"A senior analyst in Shanghai. This time you ask the questions.","role":"You are 陈琳, who graduated from the programme in 2019 and is now a senior data analyst at a large e-commerce company in Shanghai. You are candid and use workplace slang naturally (内卷, 复盘, 对齐, 赛道, 加班). Answer the advisor's questions about the job market in China, what you look for in new graduates, and what your days are like. Now and then ask how this year's students are doing."},{"id":"wellbeing","zh":"你还好吗","en":"Checking in","brief":"She has gone quiet. Find out how she is, gently.","role":"You are 小雨. You have been sleeping badly for two weeks, the job search is going poorly, and you have not told your family. You answer \"还好\" at first. You open up only if the advisor is gentle and does not rush to solutions. You are hesitant about counselling because it might make you look weak."},{"id":"free","zh":"自由聊","en":"Free chat","brief":"No scenario. Talk about anything.","role":"You are 李明, a warm, curious friend from Shanghai in your thirties who works in marketing. Chat about whatever the learner brings up: their day, their memories of Shanghai, food, work, travel, the news. Ask about their life and share small details of your own."}];
